# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Digital signatures with asymmetric key cryptography {#digital-signatures-"
"with-asymmetric-key-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Tandatangan digital dengan kriptografi kunci asimetrik {#digital-signatures-"
"with-asymmetric-key-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[*Digital "
"signatures*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191)"
" are another powerful application of asymmetric key cryptography. They "
"provide authentication, integrity, and nonrepudiation enabled by the fact "
"that within AKC, entities possess unique private keys. The basic idea "
"underlying signature protocols is that senders of secure messages will "
"additionally *digitally sign* the messages using their unique private key. "
"The receiver will then verify the digital signature using the public key of "
"the sender. Within AKC, digital signatures can be implemented by using "
"algorithms specifically designed for that purpose or by using generic "
"cryptosystems.\n"
msgstr ""
"[*Tandatangan "
"digital*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191)"
" ialah satu lagi aplikasi kriptografi kunci asimetrik yang berkuasa. Ia "
"menyediakan pengesahan, integriti, dan tanpa penolakan yang didayakan oleh "
"hakikat bahawa dalam AKC, entiti memiliki kunci peribadi yang unik. Idea "
"asas yang mendasari protokol tandatangan ialah penghantar mesej selamat akan"
" *menandatangani secara digital* mesej tersebut menggunakan kunci peribadi "
"unik mereka. Penerima kemudiannya akan mengesahkan tandatangan digital "
"menggunakan kunci awam penghantar. Dalam AKC, tandatangan digital boleh "
"dilaksanakan dengan menggunakan algoritma yang direka khusus untuk tujuan "
"itu atau dengan menggunakan sistem kripto generik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 4. Digital signatures with asymmetric key "
"cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/dig_sig_akc.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah 4. Tandatangan digital dengan kriptografi kunci "
"asimetrik](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/dig_sig_akc.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 4. Digital signatures  with asymmetric key cryptography*\n"
msgstr "*Rajah 4. Tandatangan digital dengan kriptografi kunci asimetrik*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dedicated digital signature algorithms {#dedicated-digital-signature-"
"algorithms}"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma tandatangan digital khusus {#dedicated-digital-signature-"
"algorithms}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Currently, the US Federal Information Processing Standard (FIPS) for digital"
" signatures is a dedicated scheme simply titled the [*Digital Signature "
"Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA). Somewhat similarly to the Diffie-Hellman protocol, the DSA uses the "
"algebraic properties of the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular "
"exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is raised to a power "
"(exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For example $x^e mod m$ "
".\">modular exponential</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The set of integers modulo a prime number, where the group "
"operation is modular multiplication. Elements in the multiplicative group "
"are chosen in such a way that they are coprime to the modulus, ensuring that"
" each element has a unique multiplicative inverse within the "
"group.\">multiplicative inverses</DefinitionTooltip> for signature "
"generation and verification.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada masa ini, Piawaian Pemprosesan Maklumat Persekutuan AS (FIPS) untuk "
"tandatangan digital ialah skim khusus yang dinamakan mudah [*Algoritma "
"Tandatangan "
"Digital*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA). Agak serupa dengan protokol Diffie-Hellman, DSA menggunakan sifat-"
"sifat algebra daripada <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Pemangkatan modular "
"ialah baki apabila integer dinaikkan kepada kuasa (eksponen) kemudian "
"dibahagi dengan nombor (modulus). Contohnya $x^e mod m$ .\">eksponen "
"modular</DefinitionTooltip> dan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set integer "
"modulo nombor perdana, di mana operasi kumpulan ialah pendaraban modular. "
"Elemen dalam kumpulan pendaraban dipilih sedemikian rupa sehingga ia adalah "
"koprima kepada modulus, memastikan setiap elemen mempunyai songsangan "
"pendaraban unik dalam kumpulan.\">songsangan pendaraban</DefinitionTooltip> "
"untuk penjanaan dan pengesahan tandatangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [elliptic curve digital signature "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA) is an ECC variant of DSA, providing the same functionality but with"
" significantly shorter keys. This results in improved efficiency, making it "
"a popular choice for systems with [resource "
"constraints](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"
msgstr ""
"[Algoritma tandatangan digital lengkung "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA) ialah varian ECC bagi DSA, menyediakan fungsi yang sama tetapi "
"dengan kunci yang jauh lebih pendek. Ini menghasilkan kecekapan yang lebih "
"baik, menjadikannya pilihan popular untuk sistem dengan [kekangan "
"sumber](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Both DSA and ECDSA will be illustrated in more detail later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua-dua DSA dan ECDSA akan diilustrasikan dengan lebih terperinci "
"kemudian.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Digital signature schemes using generic cryptosystems {#digital-signature-"
"schemes-using-generic-cryptosystems}"
msgstr ""
"Skim tandatangan digital menggunakan sistem kripto generik {#digital-"
"signature-schemes-using-generic-cryptosystems}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to dedicated algorithms, digital signatures can also be "
"generated using generic asymmetric cryptosystems, such as "
"[RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255).\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain daripada algoritma khusus, tandatangan digital juga boleh dijana "
"menggunakan sistem kripto asimetrik generik, seperti "
"[RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"RSA, which will be discussed in detail in a later section, also exploits "
"modular multiplicative inverses and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular "
"exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is raised to a power "
"(exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For example $x^e mod m$ "
".\">modular exponentiation</DefinitionTooltip> as fundamental operations but"
" combines them in a different sequence than DSA. In RSA, the signer "
"typically creates a hash of the message and then encrypts the hash with "
"their private key, creating the digital signature. Any party can then verify"
" this signature by decrypting it with the signer's public key and comparing "
"it with the hashed message.\n"
msgstr ""
"RSA, yang akan dibincangkan secara terperinci dalam bahagian kemudian, turut"
" mengeksploitasi songsangan pendaraban modular dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Pemangkatan modular ialah baki apabila integer dinaikkan kepada"
" kuasa (eksponen) kemudian dibahagi dengan nombor (modulus). Contohnya $x^e "
"mod m$ .\">pemangkatan modular</DefinitionTooltip> sebagai operasi asas "
"tetapi menggabungkannya dalam urutan yang berbeza daripada DSA. Dalam RSA, "
"penandatangan biasanya mencipta hash mesej kemudian menyulitkan hash "
"tersebut dengan kunci peribadi mereka, mencipta tandatangan digital. Mana-"
"mana pihak kemudiannya boleh mengesahkan tandatangan ini dengan "
"menyahsulitnya menggunakan kunci awam penandatangan dan membandingkannya "
"dengan mesej yang di-hash.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applications of asymmetric key cryptography {#applications-of-asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Aplikasi kriptografi kunci asimetrik {#applications-of-asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Asymmetric key "
"cryptography](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Public-"
"key_cryptography&oldid=1163952916) is <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Something that is present or found everywhere, or something "
"that is widespread and commonly "
"encountered.\">ubiquitous</DefinitionTooltip> in modern digital technology "
"applications. The basic functionalities of AKC described above form the "
"building blocks of many higher-level application protocols, including:\n"
msgstr ""
"[Kriptografi kunci "
"asimetrik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Public-"
"key_cryptography&oldid=1163952916) adalah <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Sesuatu yang hadir atau dijumpai di mana-mana, atau sesuatu "
"yang meluas dan sering ditemui.\">merata-rata</DefinitionTooltip> dalam "
"aplikasi teknologi digital moden. Fungsi asas AKC yang diterangkan di atas "
"membentuk blok binaan banyak protokol aplikasi peringkat lebih tinggi, "
"termasuk:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Internet communication:** Secure communication over the internet, such as "
"HTTPS, relies heavily on asymmetric key cryptography. The Transport Layer "
"Security (TLS) and its predecessor, Secure Sockets Layer (SSL), use "
"asymmetric key cryptography during the initial handshake process to "
"establish a symmetric key, which is then used for the rest of the "
"communication session.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Komunikasi internet:** Komunikasi selamat melalui internet, seperti HTTPS,"
" sangat bergantung pada kriptografi kunci asimetrik. Transport Layer "
"Security (TLS) dan pendahulunya, Secure Sockets Layer (SSL), menggunakan "
"kriptografi kunci asimetrik semasa proses jabat tangan awal untuk mewujudkan"
" kunci simetrik, yang kemudiannya digunakan untuk selebihnya sesi "
"komunikasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Authentication:** Asymmetric key cryptography is used to create digital "
"signatures, allowing an entity to authenticate a digital document or message"
" as coming from a specific sender. This is used in many scenarios, from "
"verifying software updates to legally binding digital contracts.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pengesahan:** Kriptografi kunci asimetrik digunakan untuk mencipta "
"tandatangan digital, membolehkan entiti mengesahkan dokumen atau mesej "
"digital sebagai datang daripada penghantar tertentu. Ini digunakan dalam "
"banyak senario, daripada mengesahkan kemas kini perisian kepada kontrak "
"digital yang mengikat secara undang-undang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Email encryption:** Email encryption protocols such as PGP (Pretty Good "
"Privacy) and its open-source alternative GPG (GNU Privacy Guard) use "
"asymmetric key cryptography to ensure that only the intended recipient can "
"read the email content.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Penyulitan e-mel:** Protokol penyulitan e-mel seperti PGP (Pretty Good "
"Privacy) dan alternatif sumber terbukanya GPG (GNU Privacy Guard) "
"menggunakan kriptografi kunci asimetrik untuk memastikan hanya penerima yang"
" dimaksudkan boleh membaca kandungan e-mel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Secure shell (SSH):** SSH is a protocol for secure remote login and other "
"secure network services over an insecure network. It uses asymmetric key "
"cryptography to authenticate the server to the client and, optionally, the "
"client to the server.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Secure shell (SSH):** SSH ialah protokol untuk log masuk jauh yang selamat"
" dan perkhidmatan rangkaian selamat lain melalui rangkaian yang tidak "
"selamat. Ia menggunakan kriptografi kunci asimetrik untuk mengesahkan "
"pelayan kepada klien dan, secara pilihan, klien kepada pelayan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**VPN (virtual private network):** Asymmetric key encryption is used to "
"establish secure connections in VPNs, ensuring secure communication over "
"public networks.\n"
msgstr ""
"**VPN (rangkaian peribadi maya):** Penyulitan kunci asimetrik digunakan "
"untuk mewujudkan sambungan selamat dalam VPN, memastikan komunikasi selamat "
"melalui rangkaian awam.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Blockchain and cryptocurrencies:** Blockchain technologies, including "
"Bitcoin and Ethereum, use asymmetric key cryptography. For example, the "
"ownership of Bitcoin is established through digital signatures using "
"asymmetric key cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Blokchain dan mata wang kripto:** Teknologi blokchain, termasuk Bitcoin "
"dan Ethereum, menggunakan kriptografi kunci asimetrik. Sebagai contoh, "
"pemilikan Bitcoin diwujudkan melalui tandatangan digital menggunakan "
"kriptografi kunci asimetrik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Certificate authorities:** Asymmetric key cryptography is used by "
"certificate authorities (CAs) to issue and sign digital certificates, which "
"are used in TLS communication, code signing, email encryption, and more. A "
"digital certificate binds a public key to a specific entity (for example, a "
"person or server).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pihak berkuasa sijil:** Kriptografi kunci asimetrik digunakan oleh pihak "
"berkuasa sijil (CA) untuk mengeluarkan dan menandatangani sijil digital, "
"yang digunakan dalam komunikasi TLS, penandatanganan kod, penyulitan e-mel, "
"dan lain-lain. Sijil digital mengikat kunci awam kepada entiti tertentu "
"(contohnya, seseorang atau pelayan).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 5. Issuing and signing digital certificates using asymmetric key "
"cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/ca_akc.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah 5. Mengeluarkan dan menandatangani sijil digital menggunakan "
"kriptografi kunci asimetrik](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/ca_akc.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 5. Issuing and signing digital certificates using asymmetric key "
"cryptography*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Rajah 5. Mengeluarkan dan menandatangani sijil digital menggunakan "
"kriptografi kunci asimetrik*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Security of asymmetric key cryptography {#security-of-asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Keselamatan kriptografi kunci asimetrik {#security-of-asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Several cryptographic notions come together to enable secure asymmetric key "
"cryptography, including:\n"
msgstr ""
"Beberapa gagasan kriptografi bergabung untuk membolehkan kriptografi kunci "
"asimetrik yang selamat, termasuk:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Private key secrecy**: The most basic security requirement of AKC is that "
"the private key remains secret. However, since the private key must be "
"mathematically linked to the public key, private key secrecy also requires "
"that it be computationally infeasible to derive the private key from "
"knowledge of the public key. Key generation schemes within AKC rely on "
"computationally hard mathematical problems to facilitate this requirement.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kerahsiaan kunci peribadi**: Keperluan keselamatan paling asas AKC ialah "
"kunci peribadi kekal rahsia. Walau bagaimanapun, memandangkan kunci peribadi"
" mesti dipautkan secara matematik kepada kunci awam, kerahsiaan kunci "
"peribadi juga memerlukan bahawa adalah tidak mungkin secara pengiraan untuk "
"mendapatkan kunci peribadi daripada pengetahuan tentang kunci awam. Skim "
"penjanaan kunci dalam AKC bergantung kepada masalah matematik yang sukar "
"secara pengiraan untuk memudahkan keperluan ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Trapdoor functionality** In AKC, the encryption and decryption operations "
"involve different complementary keys from a single-key pair. Ciphertext "
"generated by encryption using one of the keys (for example the public key) "
"must be inscrutable to third parties while being easily decryptable by the "
"holder of the complementary key (in this case the private key). In other "
"words, encryption should resemble a [*trapdoor one-way "
"function*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Trapdoor_function&oldid=1163913265)"
" such that third parties cannot invert the operation and recover the plain "
"text but the private key provides a secret *trapdoor* that enables easy "
"inversion. Popular AKC algorithms use modular exponentiation to set up "
"trapdoor one-way function behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Fungsi perangkap** Dalam AKC, operasi penyulitan dan penyahsulitan "
"melibatkan kunci pelengkap berbeza daripada pasangan kunci tunggal. "
"Ciphertext yang dijana oleh penyulitan menggunakan salah satu kunci "
"(contohnya kunci awam) mesti tidak dapat difahami oleh pihak ketiga manakala"
" mudah disahsulit oleh pemegang kunci pelengkap (dalam kes ini kunci "
"peribadi). Dengan kata lain, penyulitan sepatutnya menyerupai [*fungsi "
"sehala "
"perangkap*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Trapdoor_function&oldid=1163913265)"
" supaya pihak ketiga tidak boleh membalikkan operasi dan memulihkan teks "
"biasa tetapi kunci peribadi menyediakan *perangkap* rahsia yang membolehkan "
"penyongsangan mudah. Algoritma AKC popular menggunakan pemangkatan modular "
"untuk mewujudkan tingkah laku fungsi sehala perangkap.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Randomness**: The key generation process should also exploit randomness to"
" ensure that keys are unpredictable, as any pattern or predictability in key"
" generation could be exploited by an attacker. Randomness is also used for "
"padding during encryption to generate semantically secure ciphertexts and "
"within digital signature schemes to produce unique signatures even when the "
"same message is signed multiple times. For this reason, the use of strong "
"random number generators is an important part of AKC.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kerawakan**: Proses penjanaan kunci juga perlu mengeksploitasi kerawakan "
"untuk memastikan kunci tidak dapat diramalkan, kerana sebarang corak atau "
"kebolehramalan dalam penjanaan kunci boleh dieksploitasi oleh penyerang. "
"Kerawakan juga digunakan untuk padding semasa penyulitan untuk menjana "
"ciphertext yang selamat secara semantik dan dalam skim tandatangan digital "
"untuk menghasilkan tandatangan unik walaupun mesej yang sama ditandatangani "
"beberapa kali. Atas sebab ini, penggunaan penjana nombor rawak yang kuat "
"adalah bahagian penting AKC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Large key size**: As in the case of SKC, large key sizes ensure protection"
" against brute force attacks. However, since large key sizes also increase "
"the computational cost of the encryption and decryption process, an optimal "
"solution needs to balance security and efficiency considerations. The "
"following table shows typical key sizes for various asymmetric key "
"cryptography protocols and applications:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Saiz kunci besar**: Seperti dalam kes SKC, saiz kunci besar memastikan "
"perlindungan terhadap serangan brute force. Walau bagaimanapun, memandangkan"
" saiz kunci besar juga meningkatkan kos pengiraan proses penyulitan dan "
"penyahsulitan, penyelesaian optimum perlu mengimbangi pertimbangan "
"keselamatan dan kecekapan. Jadual berikut menunjukkan saiz kunci tipikal "
"untuk pelbagai protokol dan aplikasi kriptografi kunci asimetrik:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Protocol | Typical Key Sizes (in bits)         | Application                    |\n"
"|----------|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n"
"| RSA      | 1024 (deprecated), 2048, 3072, 4096 | Encryption, digital signatures |\n"
"| DSA      | 1024 (deprecated), 2048, 3072       | Digital signatures             |\n"
"| DH       | 2048, 3072, 4096                    | Key exchange                   |\n"
"| ECDH     | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Key exchange                   |\n"
"| ECDSA    | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Digital signatures             |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Protokol | Saiz Kunci Tipikal (dalam bit)      | Aplikasi                        |\n"
"|----------|-------------------------------------|---------------------------------|\n"
"| RSA      | 1024 (ditamatkan), 2048, 3072, 4096 | Penyulitan, tandatangan digital |\n"
"| DSA      | 1024 (ditamatkan), 2048, 3072       | Tandatangan digital             |\n"
"| DH       | 2048, 3072, 4096                    | Pertukaran kunci                |\n"
"| ECDH     | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Pertukaran kunci                |\n"
"| ECDSA    | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Tandatangan digital             |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Public key infrastructure**: In AKC, the private keys must be kept secret "
"by the owners while the public keys are shared. There needs to be a secure "
"mechanism to manage and distribute these public keys between users. *Public "
"key infrastructure* (PKI) provides a way to do this using *digital "
"certificates*. A digital certificate provides proof of identity of the owner"
" of the public key and is issued by a trusted authority like a certificate "
"authority(which is part of a PKI). Hence, PKI plays an integral part in the "
"security of modern application using AKC by enabling large-scale key "
"management (by creating, managing, distributing and revoking digital "
"certificates).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Infrastruktur kunci awam**: Dalam AKC, kunci peribadi mesti disimpan "
"secara rahsia oleh pemilik manakala kunci awam dikongsi. Perlu ada mekanisme"
" selamat untuk mengurus dan mengedarkan kunci awam ini antara pengguna. "
"*Infrastruktur kunci awam* (PKI) menyediakan cara untuk melakukan ini "
"menggunakan *sijil digital*. Sijil digital menyediakan bukti identiti "
"pemilik kunci awam dan dikeluarkan oleh pihak berkuasa yang dipercayai "
"seperti pihak berkuasa sijil (yang merupakan sebahagian daripada PKI). Oleh "
"itu, PKI memainkan peranan penting dalam keselamatan aplikasi moden "
"menggunakan AKC dengan membolehkan pengurusan kunci berskala besar (dengan "
"mencipta, mengurus, mengedarkan dan membatalkan sijil digital).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Security risks to asymmetric key cryptography {#security-risks-to-"
"asymmetric-key-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Risiko keselamatan kepada kriptografi kunci asimetrik {#security-risks-to-"
"asymmetric-key-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As outlined in the above table, modern asymmetric key algorithms such as RSA"
" typically employ much larger key sizes than commonly used symmetric key "
"counterparts such as AES-128. Even the ECC-based protocols (ECDH and ECDSA) "
"that have smaller key sizes employ a minimum of at least 224 bits for keys. "
"This in turn implies that a brute force attack involving an exhaustive "
"search of the private key space to identify the correct key is "
"computationally intractable in the foreseeable future. This remains true "
"even if quantum computers were to be deployed for this task. Therefore, "
"attacks against AKC usually focus on exploiting other potential weaknesses "
"of specific cryptosystems. Some well-documented attack modes target:\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang digariskan dalam jadual di atas, algoritma kunci asimetrik "
"moden seperti RSA biasanya menggunakan saiz kunci yang jauh lebih besar "
"daripada rakan sejawatan kunci simetrik yang biasa digunakan seperti "
"AES-128. Malah protokol berasaskan ECC (ECDH dan ECDSA) yang mempunyai saiz "
"kunci lebih kecil menggunakan sekurang-kurangnya 224 bit untuk kunci. Ini "
"seterusnya bermakna bahawa serangan brute force yang melibatkan carian "
"menyeluruh ruang kunci peribadi untuk mengenal pasti kunci yang betul adalah"
" tidak dapat dilaksanakan secara pengiraan dalam masa terdekat. Ini tetap "
"benar walaupun komputer kuantum digunakan untuk tugas ini. Oleh itu, "
"serangan terhadap AKC biasanya menumpukan kepada mengeksploitasi kelemahan "
"potensi lain sistem kripto tertentu. Beberapa mod serangan yang "
"didokumentasikan dengan baik menyasarkan:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Algorithmic weakness** by using sophisticated mathematical and "
"computational means to undermine the hardness assumptions used to formulate "
"asymmetric key algorithms. For example, the security of RSA is predicated on"
" the difficulty of factoring large prime numbers, and recent computational "
"advances have [enabled successful factoring of 829-bit RSA "
"keys](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)."
" Therefore, 1024-bit RSA is currently deprecated. As will be discussed "
"later, the primary risk posed by quantum computers to AKC also falls into "
"this category.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kelemahan algoritma** dengan menggunakan cara matematik dan pengiraan yang"
" canggih untuk menjejaskan andaian kekerasan yang digunakan untuk merumuskan"
" algoritma kunci asimetrik. Sebagai contoh, keselamatan RSA adalah "
"bergantung kepada kesukaran memfaktorkan nombor perdana besar, dan kemajuan "
"pengiraan terkini telah [membolehkan pemfaktoran berjaya kunci RSA "
"829-bit](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)."
" Oleh itu, RSA 1024-bit pada masa ini telah ditamatkan. Seperti yang akan "
"dibincangkan kemudian, risiko utama yang ditimbulkan oleh komputer kuantum "
"kepada AKC juga termasuk dalam kategori ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Imperfect randomness**, which can lead to weakness in the key generation "
"process. For example, if the random number generator used to create the keys"
" is flawed and generates keys that are not truly random, an attacker might "
"be able to predict the keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kerawakan tidak sempurna**, yang boleh membawa kepada kelemahan dalam "
"proses penjanaan kunci. Sebagai contoh, jika penjana nombor rawak yang "
"digunakan untuk mencipta kunci adalah cacat dan menjana kunci yang tidak "
"benar-benar rawak, penyerang mungkin dapat meramalkan kunci tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Implementation flaws** such as errors in the implementation of "
"cryptographic algorithms that inadvertently reveal information about the "
"keys. For example, incorrect padding can potentially reveal details about "
"keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kelemahan pelaksanaan** seperti ralat dalam pelaksanaan algoritma "
"kriptografi yang secara tidak sengaja mendedahkan maklumat tentang kunci. "
"Sebagai contoh, padding yang salah berpotensi mendedahkan butiran tentang "
"kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Side channels** that refer to information leakage from the physical system"
" that performs the cryptography. Such leaks could be in the form of timing "
"information, power consumption, or even sound, which can be exploited in a "
"so-called [*side-channel "
"attack*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Side-"
"channel_attack&oldid=1162235564). For example, analyzing how long "
"cryptographic operations take to execute could reveal the number of '1's in "
"a binary key. This seemingly innocent leakage significantly narrows the "
"search space, unveiling potential solutions to problems that initially "
"seemed insurmountable.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Saluran sisi** yang merujuk kepada kebocoran maklumat daripada sistem "
"fizikal yang menjalankan kriptografi. Kebocoran sedemikian boleh dalam "
"bentuk maklumat masa, penggunaan kuasa, atau bahkan bunyi, yang boleh "
"dieksploitasi dalam apa yang dipanggil [*serangan saluran "
"sisi*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Side-"
"channel_attack&oldid=1162235564). Sebagai contoh, menganalisis berapa lama "
"operasi kriptografi mengambil masa untuk dilaksanakan boleh mendedahkan "
"bilangan '1' dalam kunci binari. Kebocoran yang kelihatan tidak berbahaya "
"ini secara ketara mempersempitkan ruang carian, mendedahkan penyelesaian "
"yang berpotensi kepada masalah yang pada mulanya kelihatan tidak dapat "
"diatasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key exchange** by intercepting keys while they are being exchanged, such "
"as within a [*man-in-the-middle* "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Man-in-the-"
"middle_attack&oldid=1164741355) (MITM). The DH protocol is susceptible to "
"MITM attacks if additional authentication steps are not incorporated.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pertukaran kunci** dengan memintas kunci semasa pertukaran, seperti dalam "
"[serangan *man-in-the-"
"middle*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Man-in-the-"
"middle_attack&oldid=1164741355) (MITM). Protokol DH terdedah kepada serangan"
" MITM jika langkah pengesahan tambahan tidak dimasukkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key storage** by aiming to steal keys from poorly secured storage. This "
"includes physical attacks such as manipulation or theft of storage "
"devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Penyimpanan kunci** dengan bertujuan mencuri kunci daripada storan yang "
"tidak selamat. Ini termasuk serangan fizikal seperti manipulasi atau "
"kecurian peranti storan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Securing asymmetric key cryptosystems against the variety of attacks that "
"are possible is therefore a significant task involving mathematical, "
"hardware, software, logistical, and legal considerations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengamankan sistem kripto kunci asimetrik terhadap pelbagai serangan yang "
"mungkin adalah oleh itu satu tugas yang signifikan melibatkan pertimbangan "
"matematik, perkakasan, perisian, logistik, dan perundangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "RSA {#rsa}"
msgstr "RSA {#rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [RSA (Rivest-Shamir-"
"Adleman)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/359340.359342) algorithm is one of "
"the first public key cryptosystems and is widely used for secure data "
"transmission. It is a versatile cryptosystem in that it provides the "
"necessary operations to enable encryption, decryption, digital signatures, "
"and key exchange within a common framework.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma [RSA (Rivest-Shamir-"
"Adleman)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/359340.359342) ialah salah satu "
"sistem kripto kunci awam yang pertama dan digunakan secara meluas untuk "
"penghantaran data selamat. Ia adalah sistem kripto yang serba guna kerana ia"
" menyediakan operasi yang diperlukan untuk membolehkan penyulitan, "
"penyahsulitan, tandatangan digital, dan pertukaran kunci dalam kerangka yang"
" sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section, we will illustrate asymmetric key cryptography (AKC) using "
"RSA through simple examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam bahagian ini, kita akan mengilustrasikan kriptografi kunci asimetrik "
"(AKC) menggunakan RSA melalui contoh mudah.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will use the standard scenario of two parties, Alice and Bob, who wish to"
" communicate securely using AKC.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menggunakan senario standard dua pihak, Alice dan Bob, yang ingin "
"berkomunikasi secara selamat menggunakan AKC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The RSA algorithm {#the-rsa-algorithm}"
msgstr "Algoritma RSA {#the-rsa-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The basic RSA algorithm involves four operations: key generation, key distribution, encryption, and decryption:\n"
"1. **Key generation:**\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma RSA asas melibatkan empat operasi: penjanaan kunci, pengedaran kunci, penyulitan, dan penyahsulitan:\n"
"1. **Penjanaan kunci:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Public and private keys are generated based on mathematical principles "
"around prime numbers, where calculating them is easy, but the reverse is "
"hard.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kunci awam dan peribadi dijana berdasarkan prinsip matematik sekitar "
"nombor perdana, di mana mengira ia adalah mudah, tetapi sebaliknya adalah "
"sukar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We'll refer to these:\n"
"    - Public key: $(e, n)$\n"
"    - Private key: $(d, n)$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kita akan merujuk kepada ini:\n"
"    - Kunci awam: $(e, n)$\n"
"    - Kunci peribadi: $(d, n)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Note that $n$ is common to both public key and private key, and is known "
"as the modulus. We will need to use this later.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Perhatikan bahawa $n$ adalah biasa kepada kedua-dua kunci awam dan kunci "
"peribadi, dan dikenali sebagai modulus. Kita akan perlu menggunakannya "
"kemudian.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical detail\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Butiran matematik\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose two distinct prime numbers, $p$ and $q$.\n"
msgstr "Pilih dua nombor perdana berbeza, $p$ dan $q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "chosen at random (for security).\n"
msgstr "dipilih secara rawak (untuk keselamatan).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"They should be similar in magnitude, but differ in length by a few digits, "
"to make factoring harder.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ia sepatutnya serupa dalam magnitud, tetapi berbeza dalam panjang beberapa "
"digit, untuk menjadikan pemfaktoran lebih sukar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prime numbers can be efficiently chosen using a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An algorithm to determine whether a given number is prime. This"
" is relatively easy computationally compared to factorization.\">primality "
"test</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nombor perdana boleh dipilih secara cekap menggunakan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Algoritma untuk menentukan sama ada nombor yang diberikan "
"adalah perdana. Ini agak mudah secara pengiraan berbanding "
"pemfaktoran.\">ujian keprimeaan</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $n = p*q$.\n"
msgstr "Kira $n = p*q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$n$ is the modulus for both the public and private keys.\n"
msgstr "$n$ ialah modulus untuk kedua-dua kunci awam dan peribadi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The totient is a number, or "
"numbers, that are not greater than the given number, and are relatively "
"prime to it, having no factors in common.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\"> $φ$ </DefinitionTooltip>$(n) = (p-1)*(q-1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kira fungsi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Totient ialah nombor, atau "
"nombor-nombor, yang tidak lebih besar daripada nombor yang diberikan, dan "
"adalah perdana relatif terhadapnya, tanpa faktor yang "
"sama.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Simbol "
"Greek, phi, sering digunakan untuk menandakan totient "
"Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n) = (p-1)*(q-1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The totient is meant to be kept secret and typically discarded after key "
"generation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Totient dimaksudkan untuk disimpan secara rahsia dan biasanya dibuang "
"selepas penjanaan kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose an integer $e$ such that $1 < e < $ <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\"> $φ$ </DefinitionTooltip> $(n)$ and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole "
"numbers\">$gcd$</DefinitionTooltip>$(e, $<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The"
" greek symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)) = 1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih integer $e$ supaya $1 < e < $<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Simbol "
"Greek, phi, sering digunakan untuk menandakan totient "
"Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Pembahagi Sepunya Terbesar - nombor bulat positif terbesar yang"
" boleh membahagi dua atau lebih nombor bulat yang "
"diberikan\">$gcd$</DefinitionTooltip>$(e, $<DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Simbol Greek, phi, sering digunakan untuk menandakan totient "
"Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)) = 1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that is, $e$ and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, "
"often used to indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ "
"should be <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Two numbers that have a greatest "
"common divisor of 1. For example, 3 and 13 are coprime because only 1 can "
"divide both of them.\">coprime</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"iaitu, $e$ dan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Simbol Greek, phi, sering "
"digunakan untuk menandakan totient Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ "
"sepatutnya <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Dua nombor yang mempunyai "
"pembahagi sepunya terbesar 1. Contohnya, 3 dan 13 adalah koprima kerana "
"hanya 1 boleh membahagi kedua-duanya.\">koprima</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This number $e$ forms the public key <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"number of times a number is multiplied by "
"itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip> and is typically chosen as a small "
"number for computational efficiency.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nombor $e$ ini membentuk <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Bilangan kali "
"sesuatu nombor didarabkan dengan dirinya "
"sendiri.\">eksponen</DefinitionTooltip> kunci awam dan biasanya dipilih "
"sebagai nombor kecil untuk kecekapan pengiraan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The prime number $65537 = 2^{16} + 1$ is often used.\n"
msgstr "Nombor perdana $65537 = 2^{16} + 1$ sering digunakan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute $d$ to satisfy the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or "
"equivalence ie. all behaving in the same way.\">congruence "
"relation</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e ≡ 1 ($<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"modulus is the remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. "
"modulo is the operation of doing "
"this.\">$mod$</DefinitionTooltip><DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek "
"symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n))$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kira $d$ untuk memenuhi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Konsistensi, atau "
"kesetaraan iaitu semua berkelakuan dengan cara yang sama.\">hubungan "
"kekongruenan</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e ≡ 1 ($<DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Modulus ialah baki selepas membahagi dengan nilai yang "
"dinyatakan. modulo ialah operasi melakukan "
"ini.\">$mod$</DefinitionTooltip><DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Simbol "
"Greek, phi, sering digunakan untuk menandakan totient "
"Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n))$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '       - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, $d$ is the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Also known as "
"reciprocal, a number, which when multiplied by the number given, results in "
"a value of 1.\">multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of $e$ modulo "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Iaitu, $d$ ialah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Juga dikenali sebagai "
"salingan, satu nombor, yang apabila didarab dengan nombor yang diberikan, "
"menghasilkan nilai 1.\">songsangan pendaraban</DefinitionTooltip> $e$ modulo"
" <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Simbol Greek, phi, sering digunakan untuk "
"menandakan totient Euler.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '       - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is more efficiently computed using the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the greatest common divisor of "
"two whole numbers. It improves on the original Euclidean "
"algorithm.\">extended Euclidean algorithm</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini dikira dengan lebih cekap menggunakan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Cara cekap untuk mengira pembahagi sepunya terbesar dua nombor "
"bulat. Ia meningkatkan algoritma Euclid asal.\">algoritma Euclidean "
"lanjutan</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '       - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This number $d$ is the private key <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"number of times a number is multiplied by "
"itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nombor $d$ ini ialah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Bilangan kali sesuatu "
"nombor didarabkan dengan dirinya sendiri.\">eksponen</DefinitionTooltip> "
"kunci peribadi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The public key consists of $(e, n)$, and the private key is $(d, n)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci awam terdiri daripada $(e, n)$, dan kunci peribadi ialah $(d, n)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"2. **Key distribution:**\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"2. **Pengedaran kunci:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The public key $(e, n)$ is made public to those who may wish to send a "
"message\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci awam $(e, n)$ dijadikan awam kepada mereka yang mungkin ingin "
"menghantar mesej\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The private key $(d, n)$ is kept secret.\n"
msgstr "Kunci peribadi $(d, n)$ disimpan secara rahsia.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Encryption:**\n"
msgstr "**Penyulitan:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice wishes to send a message $M$ to Bob. In this case a simple integer\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice ingin menghantar mesej $M$ kepada Bob. Dalam kes ini satu integer "
"mudah\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice uses Bob's public key $(e, n)$ to encrypt the message into ciphertext "
"$C$\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice menggunakan kunci awam Bob $(e, n)$ untuk menyulitkan mesej menjadi "
"ciphertext $C$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical detail\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$M$ is an <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"We consider an integer in this "
"example as the simplest case. Any message can be converted into an integer "
"based representation.\">integer</DefinitionTooltip> $0 ≤ M < n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$M$ ialah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Kita menganggap integer dalam "
"contoh ini sebagai kes yang paling mudah. Mana-mana mesej boleh ditukar "
"kepada perwakilan berasaskan integer.\">integer</DefinitionTooltip> $0 ≤ M <"
" n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$C ≡ M^e (mod n)$, where $C$ is the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr "$C ≡ M^e (mod n)$, di mana $C$ ialah ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"4. **Decryption:**\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"4. **Penyahsulitan:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob receives the ciphertext $C$\n"
msgstr "Bob menerima ciphertext $C$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob uses his private key $(d, n)$ to decrypt the message back into message "
"$M$\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob menggunakan kunci peribadinya $(d, n)$ untuk menyahsulit mesej semula "
"menjadi mesej $M$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$M ≡ C^d (mod n)$.\n"
msgstr "$M ≡ C^d (mod n)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"This is the basic outline of RSA. In practice, [more sophisticated padding schemes](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577) are applied to the plain text $M$ before encryption to ensure that equal plain texts result in different ciphertexts. This prevents a range of possible attacks against naive implementations of RSA and enables <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"With only the ciphertext, and any relevant public information (such as public key for asymmetric key cryptography), and adversary cannot retrieve even partial information from the plaintext.\">semantic security</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Ini adalah garis besar asas RSA. Dalam praktik, [skim padding yang lebih canggih](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577) digunakan kepada teks biasa $M$ sebelum penyulitan untuk memastikan teks biasa yang sama menghasilkan ciphertext yang berbeza. Ini mencegah pelbagai serangan yang mungkin terhadap pelaksanaan naif RSA dan membolehkan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Hanya dengan ciphertext, dan sebarang maklumat awam yang berkaitan (seperti kunci awam untuk kriptografi kunci asimetrik), musuh tidak dapat mendapatkan maklumat separa dari teks biasa.\">keselamatan semantik</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Illustration of RSA in Python {#illustration-of-rsa-in-python}"
msgstr "Ilustrasi RSA dalam Python {#illustration-of-rsa-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following code cells, we illustrate a simple example of the RSA "
"algorithm using small integers and then demonstrate practical key "
"distribution and digital signature applications using Python libraries "
"implementing RSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam sel kod berikut, kita mengilustrasikan contoh mudah algoritma RSA "
"menggunakan integer kecil kemudian menunjukkan pengedaran kunci praktikal "
"dan aplikasi tandatangan digital menggunakan pustaka Python yang "
"melaksanakan RSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Note: In this section we will show the math calculations in detail as part of the Python code\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Nota: Dalam bahagian ini kita akan menunjukkan pengiraan matematik secara terperinci sebagai sebahagian daripada kod Python\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "RSA key generation {#rsa-key-generation}"
msgstr "Penjanaan kunci RSA {#rsa-key-generation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's step through a simple instance of the RSA algorithm employing small "
"prime numbers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita lalui contoh mudah algoritma RSA menggunakan nombor perdana "
"kecil.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will need to be able to compute the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole numbers.\">greatest common "
"divisor</DefinitionTooltip> of two integers, as it will be needed to test "
"whether two integers are <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Two numbers that "
"have a greatest common divisor of 1. For example, 3 and 13 are coprime "
"because only 1 can divide both of them.\">coprime</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita perlu dapat mengira <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Pembahagi Sepunya "
"Terbesar - nombor bulat positif terbesar yang boleh membahagi dua atau lebih"
" nombor bulat yang diberikan.\">pembahagi sepunya "
"terbesar</DefinitionTooltip> dua integer, kerana ia diperlukan untuk menguji"
" sama ada dua integer adalah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Dua nombor yang"
" mempunyai pembahagi sepunya terbesar 1. Contohnya, 3 dan 13 adalah koprima "
"kerana hanya 1 boleh membahagi kedua-"
"duanya.\">koprima</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will explain one simple way to calculate this, but it is much more "
"efficient with larger integers to use the `math.gcd` python function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menerangkan satu cara mudah untuk mengira ini, tetapi adalah lebih"
" cekap dengan integer yang lebih besar untuk menggunakan fungsi python "
"`math.gcd`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first phase of the RSA workflow is key generation. This is initiated by "
"choosing two prime numbers, which are meant to be kept secret by the entity "
"generating the keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fasa pertama aliran kerja RSA ialah penjanaan kunci. Ini dimulakan dengan "
"memilih dua nombor perdana, yang dimaksudkan untuk disimpan secara rahsia "
"oleh entiti yang menjana kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the remainder left "
"over after dividing by the value specified. modulo is the operation of doing"
" this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$, which is simply the product of the"
" two chosen primes, is computed. This modulus will be published as part of "
"the public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modulus ialah baki selepas "
"membahagi dengan nilai yang dinyatakan. modulo ialah operasi melakukan "
"ini.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$, yang merupakan hasil darab dua "
"perdana yang dipilih, dikira. Modulus ini akan diterbitkan sebagai "
"sebahagian daripada kunci awam.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Euler <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The totient is a number, or "
"numbers, that are not greater than the given number, and are relatively "
"prime to it, having no factors in common.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> "
"function <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used "
"to indicate Euler's totient.\">$\\varphi(n)$</DefinitionTooltip> is computed"
" next, as it is needed for the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an "
"integer $a$, and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the"
" case for coprimes.\">modular multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> "
"operation used to determine the keys in RSA. $phi$ is also kept secret and "
"typically discarded after key generation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Totient ialah nombor, atau nombor-"
"nombor, yang tidak lebih besar daripada nombor yang diberikan, dan adalah "
"perdana relatif terhadapnya, tanpa faktor yang "
"sama.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> Euler <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Simbol Greek, phi, sering digunakan untuk menandakan totient "
"Euler.\">$\\varphi(n)$</DefinitionTooltip> dikira seterusnya, kerana ia "
"diperlukan untuk operasi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Diberi integer $a$,"
" dan modulus $m$, baki daripada ax/m ialah 1. Ini hanya berlaku untuk "
"koprima.\">songsangan pendaraban modular</DefinitionTooltip> yang digunakan "
"untuk menentukan kunci dalam RSA. $phi$ juga disimpan secara rahsia dan "
"biasanya dibuang selepas penjanaan kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We are now ready to calculate the public and private keys. In RSA, each of "
"these is specified by a tuple of two integers. The first entry in each tuple"
" is a distinct integer, and the second entry is the modulus $n$ that is "
"common to both keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini bersedia untuk mengira kunci awam dan peribadi. Dalam RSA, setiap "
"satunya ditentukan oleh tupel dua integer. Entri pertama dalam setiap tupel "
"ialah integer yang berbeza, dan entri kedua ialah modulus $n$ yang biasa "
"kepada kedua-dua kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first entry in the public key can be any integer greater than 1 that is "
"coprime to $phi$. Two integers are coprime if their <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole numbers.\">greatest common "
"divisor</DefinitionTooltip> is 1. So we use the `math.gcd` function find an "
"integer $e$ coprime to $phi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Entri pertama dalam kunci awam boleh menjadi mana-mana integer yang lebih "
"besar daripada 1 yang koprima kepada $phi$. Dua integer adalah koprima jika "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Pembahagi Sepunya Terbesar - nombor bulat "
"positif terbesar yang boleh membahagi dua atau lebih nombor bulat yang "
"diberikan.\">pembahagi sepunya terbesar</DefinitionTooltip> mereka ialah 1. "
"Jadi kita menggunakan fungsi `math.gcd` untuk mencari integer $e$ yang "
"koprima kepada $phi$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key requires an integer $d$, which is the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Also known as reciprocal, a number, which when multiplied by "
"the number given, results in a value of 1.\">multiplicative "
"inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of $e$ modulo $phi$; that is, it satisfies the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or equivalence ie. all behaving"
" in the same way.\">congruency relation</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e\\equiv 1 "
"\\pmod{\\varphi(n)}$. For this simple illustration where we are dealing with"
" small integers, we can just loop over the positive integers to locate a "
"suitable $d$. In realistic settings, the computationally efficient "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the greatest"
" common divisor of two whole numbers. It improves on the original Euclidean "
"algorithm.\">extended Euclidean algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> is used for "
"this purpose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci peribadi memerlukan integer $d$, yang merupakan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Juga dikenali sebagai salingan, satu nombor, yang apabila "
"didarab dengan nombor yang diberikan, menghasilkan nilai 1.\">songsangan "
"pendaraban</DefinitionTooltip> $e$ modulo $phi$; iaitu, ia memenuhi "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Konsistensi, atau kesetaraan iaitu semua "
"berkelakuan dengan cara yang sama.\">hubungan "
"kekongruenan</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e\\equiv 1 \\pmod{\\varphi(n)}$. Untuk "
"ilustrasi mudah ini di mana kita berurusan dengan integer kecil, kita boleh "
"hanya mengulang ke atas integer positif untuk mencari $d$ yang sesuai. Dalam"
" tetapan sebenar, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Cara cekap untuk mengira "
"pembahagi sepunya terbesar dua nombor bulat. Ia meningkatkan algoritma "
"Euclid asal.\">algoritma Euclidean lanjutan</DefinitionTooltip> yang cekap "
"secara pengiraan digunakan untuk tujuan ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now form the tuples $(e, n), (d, n)$, which form the public and private "
"keys respectively. The public key is then published, while the private key "
"is kept secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini membentuk tupel $(e, n), (d, n)$, yang membentuk kunci awam dan "
"peribadi masing-masing. Kunci awam kemudiannya diterbitkan, manakala kunci "
"peribadi disimpan secara rahsia.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encryption and decryption in RSA use the [modular exponentiation "
"operation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Modular_exponentiation&oldid=1160764843)."
" Further, the public and private keys are complementary in that either can "
"be used to encrypt a message that the other can then decrypt.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penyulitan dan penyahsulitan dalam RSA menggunakan [operasi pemangkatan "
"modular](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Modular_exponentiation&oldid=1160764843)."
" Selanjutnya, kunci awam dan peribadi adalah saling melengkapi dalam erti "
"kata sama ada boleh digunakan untuk menyulitkan mesej yang satu lagi boleh "
"menyahsulitnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we illustrate the case where the public key $(e,n)$ is used for "
"encryption and the private key $(d, n)$ is used for decryption by defining a"
" Python function for each operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita mengilustrasikan kes di mana kunci awam $(e,n)$ digunakan untuk"
" penyulitan dan kunci peribadi $(d, n)$ digunakan untuk penyahsulitan dengan"
" mentakrifkan fungsi Python untuk setiap operasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We then encrypt and decrypt an integer message $msg$.\n"
msgstr "Kita kemudiannya menyulitkan dan menyahsulit mesej integer $msg$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the small integers used above are useful to easily outline the core "
"ideas in the RSA algorithm, in real applications RSA requires the use of "
"very large integers. For example, 2048-bit RSA involves the use of a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the remainder left over after"
" dividing by the value specified. modulo is the operation of doing "
"this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$ that is 2048 bits long, the decimal "
"integer equivalents of which are around 10$^616$. These truly enormous "
"numbers are necessary for the practical security of RSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun integer kecil yang digunakan di atas berguna untuk dengan mudah "
"menggariskan idea teras dalam algoritma RSA, dalam aplikasi sebenar RSA "
"memerlukan penggunaan integer yang sangat besar. Sebagai contoh, RSA "
"2048-bit melibatkan penggunaan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modulus ialah"
" baki selepas membahagi dengan nilai yang dinyatakan. modulo ialah operasi "
"melakukan ini.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$ yang panjang 2048 bit, "
"setara integer perpuluhan yang mana adalah sekitar 10$^616$. Nombor-nombor "
"yang benar-benar luar biasa besar ini diperlukan untuk keselamatan praktikal"
" RSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Symmetric key exchange with RSA {#symmetric-key-exchange-with-rsa}"
msgstr ""
"Pertukaran kunci simetrik dengan RSA {#symmetric-key-exchange-with-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As discussed previously, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Asynchronous key "
"encryption.\">AKC</DefinitionTooltip> enables two parties who wish to "
"communicate to securely establish a *shared secret*, which can be used, for "
"instance, as the secret key for subsequent symmetric encryption of bulk "
"plain text.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang dibincangkan sebelumnya, <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Penyulitan kunci asimetrik.\">AKC</DefinitionTooltip> "
"membolehkan dua pihak yang ingin berkomunikasi untuk mewujudkan secara "
"selamat *rahsia dikongsi*, yang boleh digunakan, sebagai contoh, sebagai "
"kunci rahsia untuk penyulitan simetrik teks biasa pukal yang seterusnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us consider the following scenario. Alice and Bob want to use "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Symmetric key "
"encryption.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip> to encrypt and decrypt messages. "
"However, before this process can be initialized, they need to agree on a "
"common secret key. One option is for one party — say, Alice — to generate a "
"secret key and then securely transmit it to Bob. To achieve this secure "
"transfer, Alice decides to use RSA as the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Key encapsulation mechanism. Secures a symmetric key by use of "
"asymmetric key encryption. A simple approach is to encrypt a random "
"symmetric key using a public key, but more advanced & secure kems are "
"available, and new ones continually developed.\">key encapsulation "
"mechanism</DefinitionTooltip> (KEM).\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita pertimbangkan senario berikut. Alice dan Bob ingin menggunakan "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Penyulitan kunci "
"simetrik.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip> untuk menyulitkan dan menyahsulit mesej."
" Walau bagaimanapun, sebelum proses ini boleh dimulakan, mereka perlu "
"bersetuju dengan kunci rahsia yang sama. Satu pilihan ialah satu pihak — "
"katakan Alice — menjana kunci rahsia kemudian menghantarnya secara selamat "
"kepada Bob. Untuk mencapai pemindahan selamat ini, Alice memutuskan untuk "
"menggunakan RSA sebagai <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Mekanisme "
"enkapsulasi kunci. Mengamankan kunci simetrik dengan penggunaan penyulitan "
"kunci asimetrik. Pendekatan mudah ialah menyulitkan kunci simetrik rawak "
"menggunakan kunci awam, tetapi KEM yang lebih maju & selamat tersedia, dan "
"yang baru sentiasa dibangunkan.\">mekanisme enkapsulasi "
"kunci</DefinitionTooltip> (KEM).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This involves the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Ini melibatkan langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Alice generates a random symmetric key, which she intends to share "
"with Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, Alice menjana kunci simetrik rawak, yang dia ingin kongsi dengan "
"Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Bob generates an asymmetric key pair and makes his public key "
"available on a suitable channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Bob menjana pasangan kunci asimetrik dan menjadikan kunci awamnya "
"tersedia pada saluran yang sesuai.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice uses Bob's public key to encrypt the symmetric key, thus "
"encapsulating it in a ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, Alice menggunakan kunci awam Bob untuk menyulitkan kunci "
"simetrik, dengan itu mengenkapsulasikannya dalam ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice broadcasts the ciphertext over a reliable but not necessarily "
"secure channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice menyiarkan ciphertext melalui saluran yang boleh dipercayai "
"tetapi tidak semestinya selamat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob receives the ciphertext and decrypts it using his private key. "
"He now has access to the symmetric key generated by Alice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, Bob menerima ciphertext dan menyahsulitnya menggunakan kunci "
"peribadinya. Dia kini mempunyai akses kepada kunci simetrik yang dijana oleh"
" Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 1. Symmetric key exchange with "
"RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/key_exchange_rsa.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah 1. Pertukaran kunci simetrik dengan "
"RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/key_exchange_rsa.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 1. Symmetric key exchange with RSA*\n"
msgstr "*Rajah 1. Pertukaran kunci simetrik dengan RSA*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Padding-based key-exchange example in Python {#padding-based-key-exchange-"
"example-in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh pertukaran kunci berasaskan padding dalam Python {#padding-based-key-"
"exchange-example-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A practical workflow utilizing RSA for padding-based non-interactive key "
"exchange is now illustrated using the ``cryptography`` Python library.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aliran kerja praktikal menggunakan RSA untuk pertukaran kunci bukan "
"interaktif berasaskan padding kini diilustrasikan menggunakan pustaka Python"
" ``cryptography``.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Import necessary modules from the ``cryptography`` Python library. If "
"needed, this library can be installed using the command ``pip install "
"cryptography``.\n"
msgstr ""
"Import modul yang diperlukan daripada pustaka Python ``cryptography``. Jika "
"diperlukan, pustaka ini boleh dipasang menggunakan perintah ``pip install "
"cryptography``.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then generates a random secret key, which she intends to transmit to "
"Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice kemudiannya menjana kunci rahsia rawak, yang dia ingin hantar kepada "
"Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the ``rsa`` module from the ``cryptography`` library, Bob generates a "
"key pair and then broadcasts his public key. Any one can intercept the "
"public key and read off the public numbers $(e,n)$ that form the key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan modul ``rsa`` daripada pustaka ``cryptography``, Bob menjana "
"pasangan kunci dan kemudiannya menyiarkan kunci awamnya. Sesiapa sahaja "
"boleh memintas kunci awam dan membaca nombor awam $(e,n)$ yang membentuk "
"kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, we assume Alice has received the public key broadcast by Bob."
" Alice's ``symmetric_key`` above can now be encrypted using Bob's public key"
" to produce the ciphertext. In a realistic setting, Alice will also use "
"additional <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The addition of data to the "
"beginning, middle, or end of a message. Often used in block ciphers to fill "
"out blocks with insufficient data up to the required "
"size.\">padding</DefinitionTooltip> methods such as "
"[OAEP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" to ensure <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"With only the ciphertext, and any"
" relevant public information (such as public key for asymmetric key "
"cryptography), and adversary cannot retrieve even partial information from "
"the plaintext.\">semantic security</DefinitionTooltip> for her "
"communications with Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada ketika ini, kita andaikan Alice telah menerima kunci awam yang "
"disiarkan oleh Bob. ``symmetric_key`` Alice di atas kini boleh disulitkan "
"menggunakan kunci awam Bob untuk menghasilkan ciphertext. Dalam tetapan "
"sebenar, Alice juga akan menggunakan kaedah <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Penambahan data ke permulaan, pertengahan, atau akhir mesej. "
"Sering digunakan dalam cipher blok untuk mengisi blok dengan data yang tidak"
" mencukupi sehingga saiz yang diperlukan.\">padding</DefinitionTooltip> "
"tambahan seperti "
"[OAEP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" untuk memastikan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Hanya dengan ciphertext, "
"dan sebarang maklumat awam yang berkaitan (seperti kunci awam untuk "
"kriptografi kunci asimetrik), musuh tidak dapat mendapatkan maklumat separa "
"dari teks biasa.\">keselamatan semantik</DefinitionTooltip> untuk "
"komunikasinya dengan Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then broadcasts the ciphertext over an open channel, confident that "
"only Bob with the corresponding private key will be able to decrypt it. We "
"assume Bob has received the ciphertext and can now decrypt it using his "
"confidential private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice kemudiannya menyiarkan ciphertext melalui saluran terbuka, yakin "
"bahawa hanya Bob dengan kunci peribadi yang sepadan akan dapat "
"menyahsulitnya. Kita andaikan Bob telah menerima ciphertext dan kini boleh "
"menyahsulitnya menggunakan kunci peribadi sulit miliknya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, Alice and Bob both have access to the secret symmetric key, "
"which they can use for <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Symmetric key "
"encryption.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip> applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada ketika ini, Alice dan Bob kedua-duanya mempunyai akses kepada kunci "
"simetrik rahsia, yang boleh mereka gunakan untuk aplikasi <DefinitionTooltip"
" definition=\"Penyulitan kunci simetrik.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simulating a Key Encapsulation Mechanism with RSA in Python {#simulating-a-"
"key-encapsulation-mechanism-with-rsa-in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Simulasi Mekanisme Enkapsulasi Kunci dengan RSA dalam Python {#simulating-a-"
"key-encapsulation-mechanism-with-rsa-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following workflow, we illustrate the use of RSA to simulate a Key "
"Encapsulation Mechanism (KEM) whereby a sufficiently long random secret "
"message is securely exchanged and subsequently converted into a shared-"
"secret of the appropriate length using a KDF.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam aliran kerja berikut, kita menggambarkan penggunaan RSA untuk "
"mensimulasikan Mekanisme Enkapsulasi Kunci (KEM) di mana rahsia rawak yang "
"cukup panjang ditukar secara selamat dan kemudiannya ditukarkan kepada "
"rahsia bersama yang sesuai panjangnya menggunakan KDF.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once again Alice and Bob want to establish a shared secret non-interactively"
" and Alice is the party that decides which secret to use.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekali lagi Alice dan Bob ingin mewujudkan rahsia bersama secara tidak "
"interaktif dan Alice adalah pihak yang memutuskan rahsia mana yang hendak "
"digunakan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We start by importing some necessary Python libraries.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mulakan dengan mengimport beberapa perpustakaan Python yang "
"diperlukan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob then generates his RSA key pair and broadcasts his public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob kemudian menjana pasangan kunci RSA-nya dan menyiarkan kunci awamnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice first generates a long random secret from which the shared secret will"
" be eventually derived. In a pure "
"[KEM](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965),"
" the long secret will be a random element from the algebraic structure "
"underlying the cryptosystem. In the case of 2048-bit RSA, this would be a "
"random integer modulo the 2048-bit RSA modulus. As such a pure KEM does not "
"require additional padding but in this example we are only simulating a KEM "
"using RSA and the `cryptography` library requires the use of padding when "
"encrypting with RSA. So we will use a somewhat shorter long secret which "
"nevertheless is much longer than a standard 256-bit AES key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice mula-mula menjana rahsia rawak yang panjang dari mana rahsia bersama "
"akhirnya akan diterbitkan. Dalam "
"[KEM](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965)"
" yang tulen, rahsia panjang itu akan menjadi elemen rawak daripada struktur "
"algebra yang mendasari sistem kriptografi. Dalam kes RSA 2048-bit, ini akan "
"menjadi integer rawak modulo modulus RSA 2048-bit. Oleh itu, KEM yang tulen "
"tidak memerlukan pengisi tambahan, tetapi dalam contoh ini kita hanya "
"mensimulasikan KEM menggunakan RSA dan perpustakaan `cryptography` "
"memerlukan penggunaan pengisi semasa penyulitan dengan RSA. Jadi kita akan "
"menggunakan rahsia panjang yang agak lebih pendek namun jauh lebih panjang "
"daripada kunci AES 256-bit standard.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next Alice encrypts the long secret using Bob's public key and the encrypted"
" secret is communicated to Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya Alice menyulitkan rahsia panjang itu menggunakan kunci awam Bob "
"dan rahsia yang disulitkan itu disampaikan kepada Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob decrypt's the encrypted secret received from Alice using his private "
"key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob menyahsulit rahsia yang disulitkan yang diterima daripada Alice "
"menggunakan kunci peribadinya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally both Alice and Bob separately apply an agreed upon [Key Derivation "
"Function](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_derivation_function&oldid=1165650237)"
" (KDF) on the long secret to derive the symmetric key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhir sekali, Alice dan Bob masing-masing secara berasingan menggunakan "
"[Fungsi Penurunan "
"Kunci](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_derivation_function&oldid=1165650237)"
" (KDF) yang telah dipersetujui ke atas rahsia panjang untuk mendapatkan "
"kunci simetri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the process involves a hashing protocol and the use of a random "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Regarding password hashing, the idea that "
"salt enhances/makes a food unique is the same idea of how adding salt in "
"this context makes our password unique, distinctive, and hard to "
"reproduce.\">*salt*</DefinitionTooltip> which ensures uniqueness and "
"unpredictability of the shared symmetric key in case the long secret is ever"
" reused (not recommended). However the *salt* itself does not have to be "
"secret and once it is randomly generated, say by Alice in this example, it "
"can be broadcasted to Bob alongside the encrypted long secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa proses ini melibatkan protokol pencincangan dan penggunaan"
" <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Regarding password hashing, the idea that "
"salt enhances/makes a food unique is the same idea of how adding salt in "
"this context makes our password unique, distinctive, and hard to "
"reproduce.\">*garam*</DefinitionTooltip> rawak yang memastikan keunikan dan "
"ketidakbolehramalan kunci simetri bersama sekiranya rahsia panjang itu "
"digunakan semula (tidak disyorkan). Walau bagaimanapun, *garam* itu sendiri "
"tidak perlu dirahasiakan dan setelah dijana secara rawak, katakanlah oleh "
"Alice dalam contoh ini, ia boleh disiarkan kepada Bob bersama rahsia panjang"
" yang disulitkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will assume therefore that both Alice and Bob have access to the same "
"random *salt*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh itu kita akan anggap bahawa Alice dan Bob mempunyai akses kepada "
"*garam* rawak yang sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Digital signatures with RSA {#digital-signatures-with-rsa}"
msgstr "Tandatangan digital dengan RSA {#digital-signatures-with-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will now extend the above confidential communication scenario with Alice "
"and Bob to one that also includes validation with the help of a [digital "
"signature](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191).\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini akan meluaskan senario komunikasi sulit antara Alice dan Bob di "
"atas kepada senario yang juga termasuk pengesahan dengan bantuan "
"[tandatangan "
"digital](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As before, Alice will confidentially send a message encapsulating a "
"symmetric key to Bob, but she will also digitally sign the message so that "
"Bob, upon receiving the message, can verify that it was Alice who originated"
" it and that the contents of the message were not tampered with during "
"transmission.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti sebelumnya, Alice akan menghantar mesej yang merangkumi kunci "
"simetri kepada Bob secara sulit, tetapi dia juga akan menandatanganinya "
"secara digital supaya Bob, setelah menerima mesej itu, boleh mengesahkan "
"bahawa Alice yang menghantar mesej itu dan kandungan mesej tidak diganggu "
"semasa penghantaran.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More generally, it is desirable to enable validation without compromising "
"confidentiality whereby any interested party is able to verify the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a message is "
"protected against unauthorized change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is "
"from the source it claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"and establish non-repudiation with respect to a given communication, even if"
" that party does not have access to the actual plain text message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lebih umum, adalah wajar untuk membolehkan pengesahan tanpa "
"menjejaskan kerahsiaan di mana mana-mana pihak yang berminat dapat "
"mengesahkan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a "
"message is protected against unauthorized "
"change.\">integriti</DefinitionTooltip>, <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">keaslian</DefinitionTooltip>, dan mewujudkan penafian "
"tidak boleh dilakukan terhadap sesuatu komunikasi, walaupun pihak itu tidak "
"mempunyai akses kepada mesej teks biasa yang sebenar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will consider this general setting which then involves the following "
"steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mempertimbangkan tetapan umum ini yang kemudiannya melibatkan "
"langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, both Bob and Alice make their public keys available over an open "
"channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, Bob dan Alice sama-sama membuat kunci awam mereka tersedia melalui "
"saluran terbuka.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice encrypts the plain text using Bob's public key, creating a "
"ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice menyulitkan teks biasa menggunakan kunci awam Bob, mencipta "
"teks sifir.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice creates a hash of the ciphertext with a *hash function* and "
"further encrypts the resulting hashed ciphertext using her private key. This"
" encrypted hash is the *signature*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, Alice mencipta cincang teks sifir dengan *fungsi cincang* dan "
"kemudian menyulitkan teks sifir yang telah dicincang itu menggunakan kunci "
"peribadinya. Cincang yang disulitkan ini adalah *tandatangan*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice then transmits both the ciphertext and the signature over an "
"open channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice menghantar kedua-dua teks sifir dan tandatangan melalui "
"saluran terbuka.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Bob uses Alice's public key to decrypt the signature, revealing the "
"hashed ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Bob menggunakan kunci awam Alice untuk menyahsulit tandatangan, "
"mendedahkan teks sifir yang telah dicincang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, since Bob also has access to the ciphertext itself, he uses the same "
"hash function used by Alice to recreate a second instance of the hashed "
"ciphertext. If the latter matches the one obtained by decrypting Alice's "
"signature, then the message is validated, even though the ciphertext itself "
"has not yet been decrypted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, kerana Bob juga mempunyai akses kepada teks sifir itu sendiri, "
"dia menggunakan fungsi cincang yang sama yang digunakan oleh Alice untuk "
"mencipta semula contoh kedua teks sifir yang dicincang. Jika yang terakhir "
"sepadan dengan yang diperoleh dengan menyahsulit tandatangan Alice, maka "
"mesej itu disahkan, walaupun teks sifir itu sendiri belum lagi "
"dinyahsulit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob, having validated the message, decrypts the ciphertext using "
"his own private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhir sekali, Bob, setelah mengesahkan mesej itu, menyahsulit teks sifir "
"menggunakan kunci peribadinya sendiri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 2. Digital signatures with RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/dig_sig_rsa.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 2. Digital signatures with RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/dig_sig_rsa.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 2. Digital signatures with RSA*\n"
msgstr "*Rajah 2. Tandatangan digital dengan RSA*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This workflow for a digital signature is illustrated next.\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja untuk tandatangan digital ini diilustrasikan seterusnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We once again import some useful modules from the ``cryptography`` library.\n"
"As before, Alice intends to securely send a symmetric key to Bob, but she also wishes to digitally sign it. In this case, we need public keys for both Alice and Bob. Therefore, the first step is for both Alice and Bob to create their own key pair using RSA and broadcast their own public key to the world.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekali lagi mengimport beberapa modul berguna daripada perpustakaan ``cryptography``.\n"
"Seperti sebelumnya, Alice berhasrat menghantar kunci simetri kepada Bob secara selamat, tetapi dia juga ingin menandatanganinya secara digital. Dalam kes ini, kita memerlukan kunci awam untuk Alice dan Bob. Oleh itu, langkah pertama adalah bagi Alice dan Bob masing-masing mencipta pasangan kunci mereka sendiri menggunakan RSA dan menyiarkan kunci awam mereka sendiri kepada dunia.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next step, as before, Alice uses Bob's public key to encrypt the "
"symmetric key and prepares the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam langkah seterusnya, seperti sebelumnya, Alice menggunakan kunci awam "
"Bob untuk menyulitkan kunci simetri dan menyediakan teks sifir.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this stage, instead of just broadcasting the ciphertext, Alice intends to"
" attach a digital signature to it so that she can prove to Bob that she was "
"the sender of the message. This is done in two steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada peringkat ini, daripada hanya menyiarkan teks sifir, Alice berhasrat "
"untuk melampirkan tandatangan digital padanya supaya dia boleh membuktikan "
"kepada Bob bahawa dia adalah pengirim mesej itu. Ini dilakukan dalam dua "
"langkah:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create a hash of the ciphertext using a hashing algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Cipta cincang teks sifir menggunakan algoritma pencincangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encrypt the hash using Alice's private key, which amounts to a signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sulitkan cincang menggunakan kunci peribadi Alice, yang merupakan "
"tandatangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then broadcasts the ciphertext and the signature over a network so "
"that Bob is able to intercept both of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice kemudian menyiarkan teks sifir dan tandatangan melalui rangkaian "
"supaya Bob dapat menerima kedua-duanya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On Bob's side, the first task is to verify the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a message is protected against "
"unauthorized change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip> of the ciphertext. To "
"do this, Bob creates a hash of the received ciphertext using the same "
"hashing algorithm used by Alice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dari sisi Bob, tugas pertama adalah untuk mengesahkan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a message is protected against "
"unauthorized change.\">integriti</DefinitionTooltip> dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">keaslian</DefinitionTooltip> teks sifir. Untuk "
"melakukan ini, Bob mencipta cincang teks sifir yang diterima menggunakan "
"algoritma pencincangan yang sama yang digunakan oleh Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Bob decrypts the received signature using Alice's public key. Because "
"Alice used her private key to create the signature, Bob is able to decrypt "
"it using Alice's public key. The decrypted signature is nothing but a hash "
"of the ciphertext created on Alice's end. If the hash created by Bob matches"
" the decrypted signature, then Bob has verified that the ciphertext he "
"received has not been tampered with and that it was Alice who signed the "
"ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Bob menyahsulit tandatangan yang diterima menggunakan kunci awam "
"Alice. Kerana Alice menggunakan kunci peribadinya untuk mencipta "
"tandatangan, Bob dapat menyahsulitnya menggunakan kunci awam Alice. "
"Tandatangan yang dinyahsulit tidak lain hanyalah cincang teks sifir yang "
"dicipta di pihak Alice. Jika cincang yang dicipta oleh Bob sepadan dengan "
"tandatangan yang dinyahsulit, maka Bob telah mengesahkan bahawa teks sifir "
"yang diterimanya tidak diganggu dan bahawa Alice yang menandatangani teks "
"sifir itu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the Python code below, these operations are combined into a useful "
"utility function called ``verify`` provided by an object associated with "
"Alice's public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kod Python di bawah, operasi-operasi ini digabungkan ke dalam fungsi "
"utiliti berguna yang dipanggil ``verify`` yang disediakan oleh objek yang "
"dikaitkan dengan kunci awam Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Having verified the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Integrity is maintained "
"when a message is protected against unauthorized "
"change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip> of the received "
"ciphertext, Bob can then decrypt it using his private key because Alice "
"created the ciphertext using Bob's public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah mengesahkan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Integrity is maintained "
"when a message is protected against unauthorized "
"change.\">integriti</DefinitionTooltip> dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">keaslian</DefinitionTooltip> teks sifir yang diterima, "
"Bob kemudian boleh menyahsulitnya menggunakan kunci peribadinya kerana Alice"
" mencipta teks sifir menggunakan kunci awam Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above digital signature scenario, any party — not just Bob — can "
"verify that Alice is the sender of the ciphertext because everyone can "
"access Alice's public key, the ciphertext, and the digital signature. "
"Furthermore, after sending the ciphertext and the signature, Alice cannot "
"later deny having done so because the signature can be decrypted to a "
"meaningful hash using only her public key. This establishes "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Non-repudiation refers to the ability to "
"prove that a specific party has sent a message. In symmetric key "
"cryptography, since the same key is used for both encryption and decryption,"
" it is not possible to determine which party has created a particular "
"ciphertext. In contrast, asymmetric key cryptography provides non-"
"repudiation through the use of digital signatures.\">non-"
"repudiation</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam senario tandatangan digital di atas, mana-mana pihak — bukan hanya Bob"
" — boleh mengesahkan bahawa Alice adalah pengirim teks sifir kerana semua "
"orang boleh mengakses kunci awam Alice, teks sifir, dan tandatangan digital."
" Tambahan pula, setelah menghantar teks sifir dan tandatangan, Alice tidak "
"boleh kemudiannya menafikan telah berbuat demikian kerana tandatangan itu "
"boleh dinyahsulit kepada cincang yang bermakna hanya menggunakan kunci "
"awamnya. Ini mewujudkan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Non-repudiation "
"refers to the ability to prove that a specific party has sent a message. In "
"symmetric key cryptography, since the same key is used for both encryption "
"and decryption, it is not possible to determine which party has created a "
"particular ciphertext. In contrast, asymmetric key cryptography provides "
"non-repudiation through the use of digital signatures.\">penafian tidak "
"boleh dilakukan</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By enabling secure key distribution and supporting non-repudiation, public "
"key cryptography establishes a strong foundation for secure digital "
"communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan membolehkan pengedaran kunci yang selamat dan menyokong penafian "
"tidak boleh dilakukan, kriptografi kunci awam mewujudkan asas yang kukuh "
"untuk komunikasi digital yang selamat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking RSA {#breaking-rsa}"
msgstr "Memecahkan RSA {#breaking-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The utility and security of the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-key"
" cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. "
"Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> algorithm outlined above rests "
"on two mathematical assumptions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kegunaan dan keselamatan algoritma <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-"
"key cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. "
"Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> yang digariskan di atas "
"bersandarkan dua andaian matematik:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finding the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and "
"modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> $d$ given "
"that access only to $(e, n)$ is computationally infeasible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mencari <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and modulus "
"$m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">songsang pendaraban modular</DefinitionTooltip> $d$ sedangkan "
"hanya mempunyai akses kepada $(e, n)$ adalah tidak boleh dilaksanakan secara"
" pengiraan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the RSA setting, the modular exponentiation operation behaves like a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A one-way function where it is easy to "
"compute an output from the inputs, but hard to determine the inputs from the"
" output.\">one-way trapdoor function</DefinitionTooltip>. When used for "
"encryption, it yields ciphertext that is inscrutable, and without access to "
"the private key, inverting the operation to recover the plain text from the "
"ciphertext is not feasible. However, with access to the private key, which "
"acts as a trapdoor, the ciphertext can be easily decrypted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam tetapan RSA, operasi pendarapan modular berkelakuan seperti "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A one-way function where it is easy to "
"compute an output from the inputs, but hard to determine the inputs from the"
" output.\">fungsi trapdoor sehala</DefinitionTooltip>. Apabila digunakan "
"untuk penyulitan, ia menghasilkan teks sifir yang sukar difahami, dan tanpa "
"akses kepada kunci peribadi, membalikkan operasi untuk memulihkan teks biasa"
" daripada teks sifir adalah tidak boleh dilaksanakan. Walau bagaimanapun, "
"dengan akses kepada kunci peribadi, yang bertindak sebagai trapdoor, teks "
"sifir boleh dengan mudah dinyahsulit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most prominent attack on the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-"
"key cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. "
"Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> algorithm aims to undermine "
"assumption 1 by efficiently recovering the private key number $d$ via "
"factorizing the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the remainder"
" left over after dividing by the value specified. modulo is the operation of"
" doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$. As will be illustrated "
"below, it is easy to recover $d$ if one has access to either the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"prime factors of a number n, are those "
"primes that are multiplied together to make n.\">prime "
"factors</DefinitionTooltip> $p$ and $q$ of $n$ or the totient "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$. Recall that $p$, "
"$q$, and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used "
"to indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ are kept secret "
"during key generation and discarded after. A third party that recovers this "
"information using a classical or quantum computer essentially uncovers the "
"private key, breaking RSA. Thus, prime factorization is the key "
"computational primitive necessary for breaking RSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Serangan paling menonjol terhadap algoritma <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A public-key cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, "
"and Leonard Adleman. Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> bertujuan "
"untuk melemahkan andaian 1 dengan memulihkan nombor kunci peribadi $d$ "
"secara cekap melalui pemfaktoran <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus"
" is the remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. modulo is"
" the operation of doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$. Seperti "
"yang akan diilustrasikan di bawah, adalah mudah untuk memulihkan $d$ jika "
"seseorang mempunyai akses kepada sama ada <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"prime factors of a number n, are those primes that are "
"multiplied together to make n.\">faktor perdana</DefinitionTooltip> $p$ dan "
"$q$ bagi $n$ atau totient <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, "
"phi, often used to indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$."
" Ingat bahawa $p$, $q$, dan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek "
"symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ dirahsiakan semasa penjanaan kunci "
"dan dibuang selepas itu. Pihak ketiga yang memulihkan maklumat ini "
"menggunakan komputer klasik atau kuantum pada dasarnya mendedahkan kunci "
"peribadi, memecahkan RSA. Oleh itu, pemfaktoran perdana adalah primitif "
"pengiraan utama yang diperlukan untuk memecahkan RSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical computing and RSA {#classical-computing-and-rsa}"
msgstr "Pengkomputeran klasik dan RSA {#classical-computing-and-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prime factorization of large integers is known to exhibit <DefinitionTooltip"
" definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for example, an exponential "
"function.\">super-polynomial</DefinitionTooltip> or <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Scaling slower than exponential. For example polynomial and "
"linear scaling.\">subexponential</DefinitionTooltip> scaling on classical "
"computers. The best-known classical algorithm for factoring integers larger "
"than $10^{100}$ is the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field "
"Sieve - An efficient classical algorithm for factoring large "
"integers.\">*general number field sieve*</DefinitionTooltip> "
"[(GNFS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=General_number_field_sieve&oldid=1151781536)\n"
msgstr ""
"Pemfaktoran perdana bagi integer besar diketahui menunjukkan penskalaan "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for "
"example, an exponential function.\">super-polinomial</DefinitionTooltip> "
"atau <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Scaling slower than exponential. For "
"example polynomial and linear scaling.\">subeksponential</DefinitionTooltip>"
" pada komputer klasik. Algoritma klasik terbaik yang diketahui untuk "
"memfaktorkan integer yang lebih besar daripada $10^{100}$ ialah "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field Sieve - An efficient "
"classical algorithm for factoring large integers.\">*penapis medan nombor "
"umum*</DefinitionTooltip> "
"[(GNFS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=General_number_field_sieve&oldid=1151781536)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="Perincian matematik">
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$L_n[\\frac{1}{3}, (\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})}] = "
"e^{[((\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})} + o(1)) "
"(log(n))^{\\frac{1}{3}}(log(log(n))^{\\frac{2}{3}})]}$\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "as a function of the integer $n$ to be factorized.\n"
msgstr ""
"$L_n[\\frac{1}{3}, (\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})}] = "
"e^{[((\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})} + o(1)) "
"(log(n))^{\\frac{1}{3}}(log(log(n))^{\\frac{2}{3}})]}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This scaling is super-polynomial in the number of bits required to represent"
" $n$.\n"
msgstr "sebagai fungsi integer $n$ yang hendak difaktorkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, prime factorization is considered inefficient on classical "
"computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penskalaan ini adalah super-polinomial dalam bilangan bit yang diperlukan "
"untuk mewakili $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Oleh itu,
# pemfaktoran perdana dianggap tidak cekap pada komp
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: </AccordionItem>
# </Accordion>
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At present, the [largest integers factored on classical "
"hardware](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)"
" are in the range of 829 bits or 250 decimal digits. Given the exponential "
"growth in classical computing power that has been witnessed over the last "
"several decades, 1024-bit RSA is no longer considered secure in the near "
"term and is now deprecated. Nevertheless, in the foreseeable future, "
"factoring 2048-bit integers whose magnitude are in the range of $10^{617}$ "
"is at present considered infeasible on classical systems, suggesting "
"continued viability. The advent of quantum computers, however, voids this "
"assessment.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shor's quantum algorithm and RSA {#shors-quantum-algorithm-and-rsa}"
msgstr "Algoritma kuantum Shor dan RSA {#shors-quantum-algorithm-and-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Probably the most well-known quantum algorithm today is <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm which can find prime factors efficiently. "
"Developed by the mathematician, Peter Shor, in 1994.\">Shor's "
"algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> for finding the prime factors of integers. "
"When [introduced by Peter Shor in "
"1994](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), it was recognized as the "
"first quantum algorithm that offered a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for example, an exponential "
"function.\">super-polynomial speedup</DefinitionTooltip> relative to "
"classical algorithms on a problem of great practical importance, namely "
"prime factorization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mungkin algoritma kuantum yang paling terkenal hari ini ialah "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum algorithm which can find prime "
"factors efficiently. Developed by the mathematician, Peter Shor, in "
"1994.\">algoritma Shor</DefinitionTooltip> untuk mencari faktor perdana "
"integer. Apabila [diperkenalkan oleh Peter Shor pada tahun "
"1994](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), ia diiktiraf sebagai "
"algoritma kuantum pertama yang menawarkan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for example, an exponential "
"function.\">percepatan super-polinomial</DefinitionTooltip> berbanding "
"algoritma klasik dalam masalah yang sangat penting dari segi praktikal, "
"iaitu pemfaktoran perdana.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm can factor primes with $O(n^2)$ where $n$ is the number of bits.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical explanation of Shor's algorithm\">\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Shor boleh memfaktorkan perdana dengan $O(n^2)$ di mana $n$ ialah bilangan bit.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Penjelasan matematik algoritma Shor\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the context of <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-key cryptosystem "
"named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. Developed in "
"1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip>, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum "
"algorithm which can find prime factors efficiently. Developed by the "
"mathematician, Peter Shor, in 1994.\">Shor's algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> "
"works by exploiting the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at "
"which a function repeats itself.\">periodicity</DefinitionTooltip> of the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when"
" an integer is raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number "
"(modulus). For example $x^e mod m$.\">modular exponential "
"function</DefinitionTooltip> $f(x) = a^x (mod~n)$ and provides a quantum "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip>-finding primitive that enables "
"efficient prime factorization of the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"modulus is the remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. "
"modulo is the operation of doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam konteks <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-key cryptosystem "
"named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. Developed in "
"1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip>, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum "
"algorithm which can find prime factors efficiently. Developed by the "
"mathematician, Peter Shor, in 1994.\">algoritma Shor</DefinitionTooltip> "
"berfungsi dengan mengeksploitasi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">keperiodikan</DefinitionTooltip> <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is "
"raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For "
"example $x^e mod m$.\">fungsi eksponen modular</DefinitionTooltip> $f(x) = "
"a^x (mod~n)$ dan menyediakan primitif pencarian <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">tempoh</DefinitionTooltip> kuantum yang membolehkan pemfaktoran "
"perdana yang cekap bagi <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the "
"remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. modulo is the "
"operation of doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simplified high-level outline of Shor's overall scheme for breaking RSA is"
" as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Garis besar ringkas peringkat tinggi skema keseluruhan Shor untuk memecahkan"
" RSA adalah seperti berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the modulus $n$, which is published as part of the public key, choose "
"a number $a$ coprime to $n$ that is, $gcd(a,n) = 1$. Since we know that $n ="
" p*q$ has exactly two prime factors $(p, q)$, almost any number less than "
"$n$ that we pick at random is likely to be coprime to $n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberi modulus $n$, yang diterbitkan sebagai sebahagian daripada kunci awam,"
" pilih nombor $a$ yang koprim kepada $n$ iaitu, $gcd(a,n) = 1$. Oleh kerana "
"kita tahu bahawa $n = p*q$ mempunyai tepat dua faktor perdana $(p, q)$, "
"hampir mana-mana nombor yang kurang daripada $n$ yang kita pilih secara "
"rawak berkemungkinan besar koprim kepada $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Having chosen $a$, find the exponent $r$ such that $a^r \\equiv 1 (mod~n)$. "
"This implies $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n)$. The existence of an "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The number of times a number is multiplied "
"by itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip> $r$ such that the above "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or equivalence ie. all behaving"
" in the same way.\">congruence</DefinitionTooltip> holds is guaranteed by "
"the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats"
" itself.\">periodicity property</DefinitionTooltip> of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is "
"raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For "
"example $x^e mod m$.\">modular exponentiation</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah memilih $a$, cari eksponen $r$ supaya $a^r \\equiv 1 (mod~n)$. Ini "
"bermaksud $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n)$. Kewujudan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The number of times a number is multiplied by "
"itself.\">eksponen</DefinitionTooltip> $r$ supaya <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Consistency, or equivalence ie. all behaving in the same "
"way.\">kongruens</DefinitionTooltip> di atas berlaku dijamin oleh "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">sifat keperiodikan</DefinitionTooltip> <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is "
"raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For "
"example $x^e mod m$.\">pendarapan modular</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $r$ is even, $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n) \\implies (a^{r/2} - 1) (a^{r/2} "
"+ 1) =  \\gamma*n$ for some integer $\\gamma$. The left-hand side of this "
"latter equality must contain $p$ and $q$ as two of its prime factors since "
"the right-hand side does. If $r$ is odd, go back to step 1 and try a "
"different choice for $a$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $r$ adalah genap, $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n) \\implies (a^{r/2} - 1) "
"(a^{r/2} + 1) =  \\gamma*n$ untuk sesetengah integer $\\gamma$. Sebelah kiri"
" persamaan terakhir ini mesti mengandungi $p$ dan $q$ sebagai dua daripada "
"faktor perdananya kerana sebelah kanan juga berbuat demikian. Jika $r$ "
"adalah ganjil, kembali ke langkah 1 dan cuba pilihan berbeza untuk $a$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the "
"greatest common divisor of two whole numbers. It improves on the original "
"Euclidean algorithm.\">extended Euclid algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> for "
"finding $gcd((a^{r/2} - 1), n)$ or $gcd((a^{r/2} + 1), n)$. The computed "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest "
"positive whole number that can divide two or more of the given whole "
"numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip>is very likely to identify one of the "
"prime factors $p$ or $q$. Divide $n$ with this prime factor to recover the "
"other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the "
"greatest common divisor of two whole numbers. It improves on the original "
"Euclidean algorithm.\">algoritma Euclid yang diperluas</DefinitionTooltip> "
"untuk mencari $gcd((a^{r/2} - 1), n)$ atau $gcd((a^{r/2} + 1), n)$. "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest "
"positive whole number that can divide two or more of the given whole "
"numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip> yang dikira sangat berkemungkinan "
"mengenal pasti salah satu faktor perdana $p$ atau $q$. Bahagikan $n$ dengan "
"faktor perdana ini untuk memulihkan yang satu lagi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once $p, q$ are known, use the steps from the original RSA algorithm for "
"reconstructing the totient $\\phi(n)$ and generating the private key number "
"$d$ as the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and modulus"
" $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of the known public key "
"number $e$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah $p, q$ diketahui, gunakan langkah-langkah dari algoritma RSA asal "
"untuk membina semula totient $\\phi(n)$ dan menjana nombor kunci peribadi "
"$d$ sebagai <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and "
"modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">songsang modular</DefinitionTooltip> bagi nombor kunci awam $e$ "
"yang diketahui.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"In August 2023 Oded Regev [published an improvement](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2308.06572) on Shor's original using a multi-dimensional approach resulting in $O(n^{1.5})$. There continues to be further research including by [Ragavan and Vaikuntanathan](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2310.00899) in this area which may improve time, cost, or number of qubits needed. Whilst we cannot say when running such algorithms against real-world RSA encryption truly becomes viable, it is becoming closer all the time.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Pada Ogos 2023 Oded Regev [menerbitkan penambahbaikan](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2308.06572) pada asli Shor menggunakan pendekatan berbilang dimensi yang menghasilkan $O(n^{1.5})$. Penyelidikan lanjut terus berlangsung termasuk oleh [Ragavan dan Vaikuntanathan](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2310.00899) dalam bidang ini yang mungkin meningkatkan masa, kos, atau bilangan qubit yang diperlukan. Walaupun kita tidak boleh mengatakan bila menjalankan algoritma sedemikian terhadap penyulitan RSA dunia nyata benar-benar menjadi boleh dilaksanakan, ia semakin hampir dari masa ke masa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Python example demonstrating breaking RSA encryption {#python-example-"
"demonstrating-breaking-rsa-encryption}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh Python yang menunjukkan pemecahan penyulitan RSA {#python-example-"
"demonstrating-breaking-rsa-encryption}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following code cells, we illustrate an example of finding a private "
"key given only the public key. This will use brute-force classical "
"computation, but shows how Shor's algorithm could be used - including large "
"keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam sel kod berikut, kita menggambarkan contoh mencari kunci peribadi "
"berdasarkan kunci awam sahaja. Ini akan menggunakan pengiraan klasik kasar, "
"tetapi menunjukkan bagaimana algoritma Shor boleh digunakan — termasuk kunci"
" yang besar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"In this section we will show the math calculations in detail as part of the Python code\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Dalam bahagian ini kita akan menunjukkan pengiraan matematik secara terperinci sebagai sebahagian daripada kod Python\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the example, we have a public key $(5, 247)$, and we will recover the "
"private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, kita mempunyai kunci awam $(5, 247)$, dan kita akan "
"memulihkan kunci peribadi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 1:** The first step is to pick a number coprime to 247. Almost any "
"number we guess will do the job. Let's pick 6.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 1:** Langkah pertama adalah untuk memilih nombor yang koprim "
"kepada 247. Hampir mana-mana nombor yang kita teka akan melaksanakan tugas "
"tersebut. Mari kita pilih 6.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 2:** Next we need to find the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"interval at which a function repeats itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip> "
"$r$ such that $6^r \\equiv 1 (mod~247)$. In this example, we compute $r$ "
"classically using brute force, but we could also use Shor's algorithm on a "
"quantum computer using <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An open-source SDK "
"for working with quantum algorithms and computers. Developed by "
"IBM.\">Qiskit</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 2:** Seterusnya kita perlu mencari <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">tempoh</DefinitionTooltip> $r$ supaya $6^r \\equiv 1 (mod~247)$. "
"Dalam contoh ini, kita mengira $r$ secara klasik menggunakan kasar paksa, "
"tetapi kita juga boleh menggunakan algoritma Shor pada komputer kuantum "
"menggunakan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An open-source SDK for working "
"with quantum algorithms and computers. Developed by "
"IBM.\">Qiskit</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 3:** Since the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which "
"a function repeats itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip> $r = 36$ is even, we"
" can compute $f1 = (a^{r/2}-1), f2=(a^{r/2}+1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 3:** Oleh kerana <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at "
"which a function repeats itself.\">tempoh</DefinitionTooltip> $r = 36$ "
"adalah genap, kita boleh mengira $f1 = (a^{r/2}-1), f2=(a^{r/2}+1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 4:** Find the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor"
" - the largest positive whole number that can divide two or more of the "
"given whole numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip> of either of those factors "
"with $n$. Simply divide $n$ with the prime factor already found to obtain "
"the second prime factor.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 4:** Cari <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor "
"- the largest positive whole number that can divide two or more of the given"
" whole numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip> bagi salah satu faktor tersebut "
"dengan $n$. Bahagikan sahaja $n$ dengan faktor perdana yang telah ditemui "
"untuk mendapatkan faktor perdana kedua.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 5:** Having recovered the prime factors of $n = 247$ as "
"$p_{found}=13$ and $q_{found}=19$, we compute the totient $\\phi_{found} = "
"(p_{found}-1)*(q_{found}-1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 5:** Setelah memulihkan faktor perdana $n = 247$ sebagai "
"$p_{found}=13$ dan $q_{found}=19$, kita mengira totient $\\phi_{found} = "
"(p_{found}-1)*(q_{found}-1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key is the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$,"
" and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of the public key number "
"$e=5$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci peribadi adalah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, "
"and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">songsang modular</DefinitionTooltip> bagi nombor kunci awam "
"$e=5$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above scheme, step 2 is the crucial <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip>-finding operation for which [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Shor%27s_algorithm&oldid=1164409434)"
" uses two fundamental quantum primitives, namely the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm that can be used to find periodic patterns."
" Named after the fourier transform in classical physics which can split a "
"signal into a set of sine waves.\">*quantum Fourier "
"transform*</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum"
" algorithm used to estimate phase in qubits, named after phase estimation in"
" classical physics.\">*quantum phase estimation*</DefinitionTooltip>. For a "
"detailed explanation of the quantum aspects of Shor's algorithm, see the "
"Phase estimation and factoring lesson in the [Fundamentals of Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms). Steps 1 "
"and 3 through 5 involve relatively inexpensive operations that can be easily"
" carried out on classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam skema di atas, langkah 2 adalah operasi pencarian <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">tempoh</DefinitionTooltip> yang penting di mana [algoritma "
"Shor](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Shor%27s_algorithm&oldid=1164409434)"
" menggunakan dua primitif kuantum asas, iaitu <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm that can be used to find periodic patterns."
" Named after the fourier transform in classical physics which can split a "
"signal into a set of sine waves.\">*jelmaan Fourier "
"kuantum*</DefinitionTooltip> dan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum "
"algorithm used to estimate phase in qubits, named after phase estimation in "
"classical physics.\">*anggaran fasa kuantum*</DefinitionTooltip>. Untuk "
"penjelasan terperinci tentang aspek kuantum algoritma Shor, lihat pelajaran "
"Anggaran fasa dan pemfaktoran dalam [Asas Algoritma "
"Kuantum](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms). Langkah 1 "
"dan 3 hingga 5 melibatkan operasi yang agak murah yang boleh dilaksanakan "
"dengan mudah pada komputer klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optionally, here's a detailed visual walkthrough of implementing [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EdJ7RoWcU48&t=325s).\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara pilihan, inilah panduan visual terperinci tentang pelaksanaan "
"[algoritma Shor](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EdJ7RoWcU48&t=325s).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On quantum computers, Shor's algorithm can exhibit <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An algorithm which scales similar to logarithmic scaling, that "
"is, efficiently compared to the size of data. A binary search is a simple "
"example.\">polylogarithmic scaling</DefinitionTooltip> as favorable as "
"$O((log~n)^2 (log~log~n))$ in terms of the modulus $n$, or "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Scales relative to a power, for example n^3."
" Grows quicker than linear scaling, but slower than "
"exponential.\">polynomial scaling</DefinitionTooltip> in terms of the number"
" of bits needed to represent $n$. This is a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial, for example an exponential "
"function.\">super-polynomial speedup</DefinitionTooltip> compared to the "
"classical <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field Sieve - An "
"efficient classical algorithm for factoring large integers.\">GNFS "
"algorithm</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada komputer kuantum, algoritma Shor boleh menunjukkan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An algorithm which scales similar to logarithmic scaling, that "
"is, efficiently compared to the size of data. A binary search is a simple "
"example.\">penskalaan polilogaritmik</DefinitionTooltip> sebaik $O((log~n)^2"
" (log~log~n))$ dari segi modulus $n$, atau <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Scales relative to a power, for example n^3. Grows quicker than"
" linear scaling, but slower than exponential.\">penskalaan "
"polinomial</DefinitionTooltip> dari segi bilangan bit yang diperlukan untuk "
"mewakili $n$. Ini adalah <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Growing faster than"
" a polynomial, for example an exponential function.\">percepatan super-"
"polinomial</DefinitionTooltip> berbanding <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"General Number Field Sieve - An efficient classical algorithm "
"for factoring large integers.\">algoritma GNFS</DefinitionTooltip> klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Recent resource estimates](https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2021-04-15-433/) indicate that based on certain "
"assumptions made regarding the hardware configuration, a few tens of "
"thousands to several million <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum bit, "
"the equivalent of a bit in classical computing. A qubit behaves very "
"differently since it can be in superposition, (imagine a combination of "
"states), but once measured the superposition collapses, and the result will "
"be 0 or 1.\">qubits</DefinitionTooltip> will be necessary to break 2048-bit "
"RSA using Shor's algorithm. It is not inconceivable that quantum computers "
"with several tens of thousands of qubits will become available over the next"
" several years, making the lower end of the resource estimate accessible.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Anggaran sumber terkini](https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2021-04-15-433/) menunjukkan bahawa berdasarkan andaian"
" tertentu yang dibuat mengenai konfigurasi perkakasan, beberapa puluh ribu "
"hingga beberapa juta <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum bit, the "
"equivalent of a bit in classical computing. A qubit behaves very differently"
" since it can be in superposition, (imagine a combination of states), but "
"once measured the superposition collapses, and the result will be 0 or "
"1.\">qubit</DefinitionTooltip> akan diperlukan untuk memecahkan RSA 2048-bit"
" menggunakan algoritma Shor. Tidak mustahil bahawa komputer kuantum dengan "
"beberapa puluh ribu qubit akan tersedia dalam beberapa tahun akan datang, "
"menjadikan hujung bawah anggaran sumber boleh dicapai.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Diffie-Hellman key exchange and the Digital Signature Algorithm {#diffie-"
"hellman-key-exchange-and-the-digital-signature-algorithm}"
msgstr ""
"Pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman dan Algoritma Tandatangan Digital {#diffie-"
"hellman-key-exchange-and-the-digital-signature-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous section, we discussed the RSA cryptosystem, whose security "
"is based on the computational hardness of prime factorization. Here, we will"
" discuss two popular asymmetric key cryptographic protocols, [*Diffie-"
"Hellman* key "
"exchange](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) and the [*Digital Signature "
"Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA), both of which are based on a different mathematical problem, namely "
"the discrete logarithm problem (DLP).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam bahagian sebelumnya, kita membincangkan kriptosistem RSA yang "
"keselamatannya bergantung pada kesukaran pengiraan pemfaktoran perdana. Di "
"sini, kita akan membincangkan dua protokol kriptografi kunci asimetri yang "
"popular, iaitu [pertukaran kunci *Diffie-"
"Hellman*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) dan [*Algoritma Tandatangan "
"Digital*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA), kedua-duanya berasaskan masalah matematik yang berbeza, iaitu "
"masalah logaritma diskret (DLP).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The discrete logarithm problem {#the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah logaritma diskret {#the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the following equation we need to find $a$ given only $e$,$M$,$c$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam persamaan berikut, kita perlu mencari $a$ dengan hanya diberi $e$, "
"$M$, $c$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$a^e$ $mod$ $M = c$\n"
msgstr "$a^e$ $mod$ $M = c$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is believed to be difficult with classic computers due to the use of "
"modulo arithmetic, and therefore is a good mathematical basis for an "
"encryption algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini dipercayai sukar dilakukan dengan komputer klasik kerana penggunaan "
"aritmetik modulo, dan oleh itu menjadi asas matematik yang baik untuk "
"algoritma penyulitan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is known as the [discrete logarithm "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Discrete_logarithm&oldid=1161792952)"
" (DLP).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini dikenali sebagai [masalah logaritma "
"diskret](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Discrete_logarithm&oldid=1161792952)"
" (DLP).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mathematical details of the discrete logarithm problem {#mathematical-"
"details-of-the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Butiran matematik masalah logaritma diskret {#mathematical-details-of-the-"
"discrete-logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The DLP is typically framed in the context of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Group where all elements are generated by repeatedly applying a"
" single element, known as a generator. This process creates a cycle of "
"elements that closes upon itself.\">cyclic groups</DefinitionTooltip> and is"
" stated as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"DLP biasanya dibingkai dalam konteks <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Kumpulan di mana semua elemen dijana dengan menerapkan satu "
"elemen tunggal secara berulang, dikenali sebagai penjana. Proses ini "
"mencipta kitaran elemen yang menutup dengan sendirinya.\">kumpulan "
"kitaran</DefinitionTooltip> dan dinyatakan seperti berikut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider a [cyclic "
"group](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cyclic_group&oldid=1150017831)"
" $G$ generated by a group element $g \\in G$ and given an arbitrary element "
"$h \\in G$, find an integer $k$ such that $h = g^{k}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan [kumpulan "
"kitaran](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cyclic_group&oldid=1150017831)"
" $G$ yang dijana oleh elemen kumpulan $g \\in G$ dan diberi elemen "
"sembarangan $h \\in G$, cari integer $k$ supaya $h = g^{k}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here the integer $k \\equiv log_{g}h$ is the discrete logarithm. The cyclic "
"property of $G$ guarantees that for every $h$, a valid integer $k$ exists.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini integer $k \\equiv log_{g}h$ adalah logaritma diskret. Sifat kitaran"
" $G$ menjamin bahawa untuk setiap $h$, terdapat integer $k$ yang sah.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For cryptography, the DLP on the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The set of "
"integers modulo a prime number, where the group operation is modular "
"multiplication. Elements in the multiplicative group are chosen in such a "
"way that they are coprime to the modulus, ensuring that each element has a "
"unique multiplicative inverse within the group.\">multiplicative "
"group</DefinitionTooltip> of integers modulo a prime number $p$ denoted "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ turns out to be useful. The elements of "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ are congruence classes labeled by integers "
"modulo $p$ that are coprime to $p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk kriptografi, DLP pada <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set integer "
"modulo nombor perdana, di mana operasi kumpulan adalah pendaraban modular. "
"Elemen dalam kumpulan pendaraban dipilih supaya coprime dengan modulus, "
"memastikan setiap elemen mempunyai songsangan pendaraban yang unik dalam "
"kumpulan tersebut.\">kumpulan pendaraban</DefinitionTooltip> integer modulo "
"nombor perdana $p$ yang ditandakan $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ ternyata "
"berguna. Elemen-elemen $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ ialah kelas kongruens "
"yang dilabelkan dengan integer modulo $p$ yang coprime dengan $p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For example:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_5)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4]\\}~\\mathrm{and}~(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4],[5],[6]\\} $\n"
msgstr ""
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_5)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4]\\}~\\mathrm{and}~(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4],[5],[6]\\} $\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation of multiplication $(\\times)$ on these groups is simply "
"ordinary integer multiplication followed by reduction modulo $p$ and "
"exponentiation by an integer $k$ is just repeated multiplication $k$ times "
"and reduction modulo $p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi pendaraban $(\\times)$ pada kumpulan ini hanyalah pendaraban integer"
" biasa diikuti dengan pengurangan modulo $p$, dan pemangkatan dengan integer"
" $k$ hanyalah pendaraban berulang sebanyak $k$ kali dan pengurangan modulo "
"$p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's illustrate an instance of the DLP on $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$.\n"
msgstr "Mari kita ilustrasikan contoh DLP pada $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This multiplicative group has two generators ${[3],[5]}$ also known as "
"primitive roots. We will use $[5]$ as the generator; that is, generate every"
" element of $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ using successive integer powers of "
"5.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kumpulan pendaraban ini mempunyai dua penjana ${[3],[5]}$ yang juga dikenali"
" sebagai punca primitif. Kita akan menggunakan $[5]$ sebagai penjana; iaitu,"
" jana setiap elemen $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ menggunakan kuasa integer "
"berturutan bagi 5.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that in modulo 7 arithmetic, raising 5 to successive integer powers "
"yields every element of $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ exactly once before the "
"cycle repeats indefinitely with a period $p-1 =6$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita lihat bahawa dalam aritmetik modulo 7, menaikkan 5 kepada kuasa integer"
" berturutan menghasilkan setiap elemen $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ tepat "
"sekali sebelum kitaran berulang tanpa had dengan tempoh $p-1 =6$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "So the DLP on $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ with generator [5] is:\n"
msgstr "Jadi DLP pada $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ dengan penjana [5] ialah:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ \\mathrm{Given}~h \\in (\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} \\mathrm{, find~} k "
"\\mathrm{~such~that~} 5^{k} \\equiv h~(mod~7)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ \\mathrm{Given}~h \\in (\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} \\mathrm{, find~} k "
"\\mathrm{~such~that~} 5^{k} \\equiv h~(mod~7)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "From the above Python cell output we see that:\n"
msgstr "Daripada output sel Python di atas kita lihat bahawa:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$h = 2 \\implies k=4 \\mathrm{~or~}  4 = log_5(2) (mod~7)$\n"
msgstr "$h = 2 \\implies k=4 \\mathrm{~or~}  4 = log_5(2) (mod~7)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$h = 6 \\implies k=3 \\mathrm{~or~}  3 = log_5(6) (mod~7)$\n"
msgstr "$h = 6 \\implies k=3 \\mathrm{~or~}  3 = log_5(6) (mod~7)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In ordinary real number arithmetic, exponentiation is a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A behavior or relationship that consistently moves in a single "
"direction without reversals; for example in a monotonically increasing "
"function, values consistently increase.\">monotonic</DefinitionTooltip> "
"function and finding the logarithm of any number to any base is "
"computationally easy. In contrast, as is apparent from the simple "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ example above, modular exponentiation is non-"
"monotonic, and even though it is periodic with period $p-1$, it is otherwise"
" highly nontrivial. So computing its inverse, the discrete logarithm turns "
"out to be inefficient for large $p$ on classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam aritmetik nombor nyata biasa, pemangkatan adalah fungsi "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Tingkah laku atau hubungan yang konsisten "
"bergerak dalam satu arah tanpa pembalikan; contohnya dalam fungsi menoton "
"meningkat, nilai konsisten bertambah.\">monoton</DefinitionTooltip> dan "
"mencari logaritma sebarang nombor kepada sebarang asas adalah mudah secara "
"pengiraan. Sebaliknya, seperti yang jelas daripada contoh mudah "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ di atas, pemangkatan modular adalah bukan "
"monoton, dan walaupun ia berkala dengan tempoh $p-1$, ia sebaliknya sangat "
"tidak trivial. Jadi mengira songsangannya, iaitu logaritma diskret, ternyata"
" tidak cekap untuk $p$ yang besar pada komputer klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This observation underpins both Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange and the "
"Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA), which are discussed in the next "
"section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pemerhatian ini menyokong kedua-dua pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman (DH) dan"
" Algoritma Tandatangan Digital (DSA), yang dibincangkan dalam bahagian "
"seterusnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The DLP can be extended to cyclic subgroups as follows:\n"
msgstr "DLP boleh diperluaskan kepada subkumpulan kitaran seperti berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ defined above and an element $g \\in "
"(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ of prime order $r$ that is, $g^r \\equiv 1 "
"(~mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ yang ditakrifkan di atas dan "
"elemen $g \\in (\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ bertertib perdana $r$, iaitu $g^r "
"\\equiv 1 (~mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The set of integer powers of $g$: $\\{g^k~(mod~p) | 1 \\le k \\le r\\} = "
"\\langle g \\rangle$ is a cyclic subgroup of $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ "
"with group order $r$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Set kuasa integer bagi $g$: $\\{g^k~(mod~p) | 1 \\le k \\le r\\} = \\langle "
"g \\rangle$ adalah subkumpulan kitaran $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ dengan "
"tertib kumpulan $r$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A DLP can be specified on $\\langle g \\rangle$ by choosing a $h \\in "
"\\langle g \\rangle$ and asking for $1 \\le a \\le r$ such that $ "
"g^a~(mod~p) = h$\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu DLP boleh ditentukan pada $\\langle g \\rangle$ dengan memilih $h \\in "
"\\\\langle g \\rangle$ dan meminta $1 \\le a \\le r$ supaya $ g^a~(mod~p) = "
"h$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Diffie-Hellman key exchange {#diffie-hellman-key-exchange}"
msgstr "Pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman {#diffie-hellman-key-exchange}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In 1976, [Whitfield Diffie and Martin Hellman proposed a key exchange "
"protocol](https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1976.1055638) to enable the creation "
"of a shared secret key over insecure communication channels. The secret key "
"could then be used by parties sharing it for symmetric encryption. The "
"algorithm relies on the DLP.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 1. Diffie-Hellman key exchange](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/key_exchange_dh.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada tahun 1976, [Whitfield Diffie dan Martin Hellman mencadangkan protokol "
"pertukaran kunci](https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1976.1055638) untuk "
"membolehkan penciptaan kunci rahsia dikongsi melalui saluran komunikasi yang"
" tidak selamat. Kunci rahsia tersebut kemudian boleh digunakan oleh pihak-"
"pihak yang berkongsinya untuk penyulitan simetri. Algoritma ini bergantung "
"pada DLP.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 1. Diffie-Hellman key exchange*\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah 1. Pertukaran kunci Diffie-"
"Hellman](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/key_exchange_dh.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: *Rajah 1.
# Pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman*
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="Butiran matematik pertukar
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of Diffie-Hellman key "
"exchange\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With Alice and Bob being the two parties communicating, the protocol works "
"as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan Alice dan Bob sebagai dua pihak yang berkomunikasi, protokol "
"berfungsi seperti berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Alice and Bob agree on a large prime number $p$ and a primitive root "
"or generator $a$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, Alice dan Bob bersetuju pada nombor perdana besar $p$ dan punca "
"primitif atau penjana $a$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice chooses a secret exponent $k_A$ randomly with $1 \\le k_A \\le "
"p-2$ and calculates $h_A = a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. $k_A, h_A$ are Alice's  private"
" and public keys respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice memilih eksponen rahsia $k_A$ secara rawak dengan $1 \\le "
"k_A \\le p-2$ dan mengira $h_A = a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. $k_A, h_A$ masing-masing "
"adalah kunci peribadi dan kunci awam Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Bob chooses a secret exponent $k_B$ randomly with  $1 \\le k_B \\le "
"p-2$ and calculates $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$. $k_B, h_B$ are Bob's  private "
"and public keys respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, Bob memilih eksponen rahsia $k_B$ secara rawak dengan $1 \\le "
"k_B \\le p-2$ dan mengira $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$. $k_B, h_B$ masing-masing "
"adalah kunci peribadi dan kunci awam Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice sends Bob $h_A$ and Bob sends Alice $h_B$ over a reliable but "
"not necessarily secure channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, Alice menghantar $h_A$ kepada Bob dan Bob menghantar $h_B$ kepada "
"Alice melalui saluran yang boleh dipercayai tetapi tidak semestinya "
"selamat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice then uses the $h_B$ she received to compute the shared secret "
"key $ \\kappa = h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selepas itu, Alice menggunakan $h_B$ yang diterimanya untuk mengira kunci "
"rahsia dikongsi $ \\kappa = h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob meanwhile uses the $h_A$ he received to compute the shared "
"secret key $ \\kappa = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, Bob pula menggunakan $h_A$ yang diterimanya untuk mengira kunci "
"rahsia dikongsi $ \\kappa = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "With this protocol,\n"
msgstr "Dengan protokol ini,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob are guaranteed to end up with the same secret key $\\kappa$ "
"because $h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p) = (a^{k_B})^{k_A}~(mod~p) = a^{k_A k_B}~(mod~p) ="
" (a^{k_A})^{k_B}~(mod~p) = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p) $.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice dan Bob dijamin berakhir dengan kunci rahsia yang sama $\\kappa$ "
"kerana $h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p) = (a^{k_B})^{k_A}~(mod~p) = a^{k_A k_B}~(mod~p) = "
"(a^{k_A})^{k_B}~(mod~p) = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p) $.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A third party that intercepts $h_A$ or $h_B$ cannot construct the secret key"
" $\\kappa$ because they do not have access to $k_B$ or $k_A$ respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pihak ketiga yang memintas $h_A$ atau $h_B$ tidak boleh membina kunci rahsia"
" $\\kappa$ kerana mereka tidak mempunyai akses kepada $k_B$ atau $k_A$ "
"masing-masing.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Extracting $k_A$ or $k_B$ using the public information $a$, $p$, $h_A$ and "
"$h_B$ is computationally hard as it is equivalent to solving the DLP on "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengekstrak $k_A$ atau $k_B$ menggunakan maklumat awam $a$, $p$, $h_A$ dan "
"$h_B$ adalah sukar secara pengiraan kerana ia bersamaan dengan menyelesaikan"
" DLP pada $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Illustration of the Diffie-Hellman protocol in Python {#illustration-of-the-"
"diffie-hellman-protocol-in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Ilustrasi protokol Diffie-Hellman dalam Python {#illustration-of-the-diffie-"
"hellman-protocol-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's look at a simple example of the DH protocol in Python using small "
"prime numbers:\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita lihat contoh mudah protokol DH dalam Python menggunakan nombor "
"perdana kecil:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 1:** Alice and Bob agree on a prime $p$ and a primitive root $a$. "
"Let's choose $p=11, a=7$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 1:** Alice dan Bob bersetuju pada perdana $p$ dan punca primitif "
"$a$. Mari pilih $p=11, a=7$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Steps 2, 3:** Alice chooses a secret exponent $k_A$ and calculates $h_A = "
"a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. Similarly, Bob chooses a secret exponent $k_B$ and "
"calculates $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 2, 3:** Alice memilih eksponen rahsia $k_A$ dan mengira $h_A = "
"a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. Begitu juga, Bob memilih eksponen rahsia $k_B$ dan mengira"
" $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 4:** The two parties broadcast their public keys $h_A$ and $h_B$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 4:** Kedua-dua pihak menyiarkan kunci awam mereka $h_A$ dan "
"$h_B$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Steps 5, 6:** Each party combines their private key with the other party's"
" public key to create the shared secret key.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Langkah 5, 6:** Setiap pihak menggabungkan kunci peribadi mereka dengan "
"kunci awam pihak lain untuk mencipta kunci rahsia dikongsi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can now use the shared secret key for symmetric encryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice dan Bob kini boleh menggunakan kunci rahsia dikongsi untuk penyulitan "
"simetri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Security of Diffie-Hellman key exchange {#security-of-diffie-hellman-key-"
"exchange}"
msgstr ""
"Keselamatan pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman {#security-of-diffie-hellman-"
"key-exchange}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As noted above, the security of DH is predicated on the computational "
"difficulty of solving the DLP with large primes $p$. In typical "
"applications, NIST recommends 2048- or 3072-bit prime integers for DH key "
"exchange, which is considered sufficiently secure against attempts to solve "
"the DLP using classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang dinyatakan di atas, keselamatan DH bergantung pada kesukaran "
"pengiraan menyelesaikan DLP dengan perdana besar $p$. Dalam aplikasi biasa, "
"NIST mengesyorkan integer perdana 2048 atau 3072 bit untuk pertukaran kunci "
"DH, yang dianggap cukup selamat terhadap percubaan menyelesaikan DLP "
"menggunakan komputer klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks**: The fact that DH is an interactive "
"scheme where the shared secret depends on combining one party's private key "
"with the other party's public key makes it vulnerable to a so-called *Man-"
"in-the-middle (MITM)* attack.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Serangan Man-in-the-middle (MITM)**: Hakikat bahawa DH adalah skim "
"interaktif di mana rahsia dikongsi bergantung pada penggabungan kunci "
"peribadi satu pihak dengan kunci awam pihak lain menjadikannya terdedah "
"kepada serangan yang dipanggil *Man-in-the-middle (MITM)*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="Butiran matematik keselama
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of DH security and MITM "
"attacks\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this scenario, a third party — say, Eve — intercepts the public keys "
"$h_A, h_B$ during transmission and substitutes her own public key $h_E$ for "
"each of $h_A$ and $h_B$ before forwarding them along to Bob and Alice, "
"respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam senario ini, pihak ketiga — katakanlah, Eve — memintas kunci awam "
"$h_A, h_B$ semasa penghantaran dan menggantikan kunci awamnya sendiri $h_E$ "
"untuk setiap $h_A$ dan $h_B$ sebelum meneruskannya kepada Bob dan Alice "
"masing-masing.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, instead of using $h_B$ to create her shared secret, Alice will use "
"$h_E$ while thinking that she is using Bob's public key. Similarly, instead "
"of using $h_A$ to create his shared secret, Bob will use $h_E$ while "
"thinking that he is using Alice's public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemudian, bukannya menggunakan $h_B$ untuk mencipta rahsia berkongsiannya, "
"Alice akan menggunakan $h_E$ sambil menyangka bahawa dia menggunakan kunci "
"awam Bob. Begitu juga, bukannya menggunakan $h_A$ untuk mencipta rahsia "
"berkongsiannya, Bob akan menggunakan $h_E$ sambil menyangka bahawa dia "
"menggunakan kunci awam Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $h_E$ was used to create Alice's (Bob's) shared secret, plain text "
"encrypted by Alice (Bob) can be decrypted by Eve.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kerana $h_E$ digunakan untuk mencipta rahsia dikongsi Alice (Bob), teks "
"biasa yang disulitkan oleh Alice (Bob) boleh dinyahsulit oleh Eve.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, DH key exchange is typically used in conjunction with a digital "
"signature algorithm to ensure that each party uses an authenticated public "
"key for creating their shared secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh itu, pertukaran kunci DH biasanya digunakan bersama algoritma "
"tandatangan digital untuk memastikan setiap pihak menggunakan kunci awam "
"yang telah disahkan untuk mencipta rahsia dikongsi mereka.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA) {#the-digital-signature-algorithm-dsa}"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Tandatangan Digital (DSA) {#the-digital-signature-algorithm-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Even though generic cryptosystems like [RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255) provide digital signature functionality, in 1994 NIST adopted a specialized signature scheme based on modular exponentiation and the discrete logarithm problem as the federal standard for digital signatures. This scheme, which came to be known simply as the [*Digital Signature Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522) (DSA), involves four distinct phases:\n"
"1. **Key generation**:\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun kriptosistem generik seperti [RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255) menyediakan fungsi tandatangan digital, pada tahun 1994 NIST mengadopsi skim tandatangan khusus berdasarkan pemangkatan modular dan masalah logaritma diskret sebagai piawaian persekutuan untuk tandatangan digital. Skim ini, yang kemudian dikenali hanya sebagai [*Algoritma Tandatangan Digital*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522) (DSA), melibatkan empat fasa berbeza:\n"
"1. **Penjanaan kunci**:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   DSA keys are generated from:\n"
"     - 2 primes that meet certain rules\n"
"       -   $p$ - typically 256 bits (we'll call this length $N$)\n"
"       -   $q$ - typically 3072 bits (we'll call this length $L$)\n"
"     - A cryptographic hash function that will convert from strings of length $L$ to $N$\n"
"     - An additional Parameters $g$ (see details below)\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kunci DSA dijana daripada:\n"
"     - 2 nombor perdana yang memenuhi peraturan tertentu\n"
"       -   $p$ - biasanya 256 bit (kita panggil panjang ini $N$)\n"
"       -   $q$ - biasanya 3072 bit (kita panggil panjang ini $L$)\n"
"     - Fungsi cincang kriptografi yang akan menukar daripada rentetan panjang $L$ kepada $N$\n"
"     - Parameter tambahan $g$ (lihat butiran di bawah)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   From this we choose a random number $x$ as private key, and are able to "
"calculate a public key $y$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Daripada ini kita memilih nombor rawak $x$ sebagai kunci peribadi, dan "
"mampu mengira kunci awam $y$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of key generation\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Butiran matematik penjanaan kunci\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Parameter generation:** Mathematically, DSA involves a cyclic subgroup of "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ generated by an element $g$ of prime order q < "
"p. The first step in the DSA is therefore to select two primes p, q to set "
"up the necessary mathematical structures.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Penjanaan parameter:** Secara matematik, DSA melibatkan subkumpulan "
"kitaran $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ yang dijana oleh elemen $g$ bertertib "
"perdana q < p. Langkah pertama dalam DSA adalah memilih dua nombor perdana "
"p, q untuk menyediakan struktur matematik yang diperlukan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose an $N$-bit prime $q$.\n"
msgstr "Pilih nombor perdana $q$ sebanyak $N$ bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose an $L$-bit prime $p$ such that $p-1$ is a multiple of $q$. The choice"
" of $p$ specifies the group $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih nombor perdana $p$ sebanyak $L$ bit supaya $p-1$ adalah gandaan $q$. "
"Pilihan $p$ menentukan kumpulan $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pick an integer $1 < h < p-1$ at random and compute $g = h^{(p-1)/q}~mod~p$."
" If $g=1$ which happens rarely, try another h.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ambil integer $1 < h < p-1$ secara rawak dan kira $g = h^{(p-1)/q}~mod~p$. "
"Jika $g=1$ yang jarang berlaku, cuba $h$ yang lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Verify that $g^q~mod~p = 1$. g is thus a generator of a cyclic subgroup "
"$\\langle g \\rangle$ of $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ of prime order q.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sahkan bahawa $g^q~mod~p = 1$. g dengan itu adalah penjana subkumpulan "
"kitaran $\\langle g \\rangle$ bagi $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ bertertib "
"perdana q.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     The parameters $(q, p, g)$ specify an instance of the algorithm and are"
" public information. Typically, $ N \\sim 256$ and $L \\sim 3072$ in "
"realistic applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"     Parameter $(q, p, g)$ menentukan contoh algoritma dan merupakan "
"maklumat awam. Biasanya, $ N \\sim 256$ dan $L \\sim 3072$ dalam aplikasi "
"sebenar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     The protocol also requires a cryptographic hash function $H : "
"\\{0,1\\}^L \\rightarrow \\{0, 1\\}^N$ that maps binary $L$-bit strings to "
"$N$-bit strings, for example, SHA-256.\n"
msgstr ""
"     Protokol ini juga memerlukan fungsi cincang kriptografi $H : "
"\\{0,1\\}^L \\rightarrow \\{0, 1\\}^N$ yang memetakan rentetan binari $L$ "
"bit kepada rentetan $N$ bit, contohnya, SHA-256.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key-pair generation:** The signer needs to generate a key pair on their "
"end.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Penjanaan pasangan kunci:** Penandatangan perlu menjana pasangan kunci di "
"pihak mereka.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a random secret integer $ x \\in \\{1,2...q-1\\}$. $x$ is the private"
" key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih integer rahsia rawak $ x \\in \\{1,2...q-1\\}$. $x$ adalah kunci "
"peribadi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate $ y = g^{x}~mod~p$. $y$ is the signer's public key.\n"
msgstr "Jana $ y = g^{x}~mod~p$. $y$ adalah kunci awam penandatangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The following information is shared with anyone who wishes to validate a signature\n"
"   - The parameters used $(p,q,g)$ which describe the algorithm\n"
"   - The hash function $H$\n"
"   - the public key $y$\n"
"1. **Signing:**\n"
msgstr ""
"   Maklumat berikut dikongsi dengan sesiapa yang ingin mengesahkan tandatangan\n"
"   - Parameter yang digunakan $(p,q,g)$ yang menerangkan algoritma\n"
"   - Fungsi cincang $H$\n"
"   - Kunci awam $y$\n"
"1. **Penandatanganan:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The signer can now sign a message $m$. The resulting signature is $(r,s)$\n"
msgstr ""
"Penandatangan kini boleh menandatangani mesej $m$. Tandatangan yang "
"dihasilkan adalah $(r,s)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The message and signature are both now sent to the recipient\n"
msgstr "Mesej dan tandatangan kedua-duanya kini dihantar kepada penerima\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of signing a message\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Butiran matematik menandatangani mesej\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   The signer signs a message $m$ as follows:\n"
msgstr "   Penandatangan menandatangani mesej $m$ seperti berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a secret integer k at random from $\\{1,2...q-1\\}$\n"
msgstr "Pilih integer rahsia k secara rawak daripada $\\{1,2...q-1\\}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute $r = (g^k~mod~p)~mod~q$. In the rare instance when $r=0$, try "
"another random k.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kira $r = (g^k~mod~p)~mod~q$. Dalam kes yang jarang berlaku apabila $r=0$, "
"cuba k rawak yang lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q$. In a rare instances if $s=0$, try "
"another random k.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kira $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q$. Dalam kes yang jarang berlaku jika "
"$s=0$, cuba k rawak yang lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The signature is the tuple $(r, s)$.\n"
msgstr "Tandatangan adalah tuple $(r, s)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The signer transmits the message $m$ as well as the signature $(r,s)$ to the"
" verifier.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penandatangan menghantar mesej $m$ serta tandatangan $(r,s)$ kepada "
"pengesah.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Because both $r, s$ are integers, modulo $q$ the signature size is on the"
" order of $N$-bits and not the longer $L$-bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Kerana kedua-dua $r, s$ adalah integer, modulo $q$ saiz tandatangan "
"adalah dalam tertib $N$ bit dan bukan $L$ bit yang lebih panjang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"2. **Verification:**\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"2. **Pengesahan:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The recipient now wishes to verify the authenticity of the sender.\n"
"   They have access to the public information $(q, p, g, H, y, (r,s), m)$\n"
"   They can execute a calculation which proves that the sender had access to the private key $x$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Penerima kini ingin mengesahkan kesahihan penghantar.\n"
"   Mereka mempunyai akses kepada maklumat awam $(q, p, g, H, y, (r,s), m)$\n"
"   Mereka boleh melaksanakan pengiraan yang membuktikan bahawa penghantar mempunyai akses kepada kunci peribadi $x$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   and seeks to ascertain that the signer is someone with access to the "
"private key $x$.\n"
msgstr ""
"   dan berusaha memastikan bahawa penandatangan adalah seseorang yang "
"mempunyai akses kepada kunci peribadi $x$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of DSA verification scheme\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Butiran matematik skim pengesahan DSA\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Verify that $0 \\lt r \\lt q$ and $0 \\lt s \\lt q$, that is, $r, s$ are "
"valid modulo~q integers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sahkan bahawa $0 \\lt r \\lt q$ dan $0 \\lt s \\lt q$, iaitu, $r, s$ adalah "
"integer modulo~q yang sah.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Kira $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Kira $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $u_2 = rw~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Kira $u_2 = rw~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Kira $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The signature is verified if $v = r$.\n"
msgstr "Tandatangan disahkan jika $v = r$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For legitimate signatures, the correctness of the DSA algorithm is easily"
" demonstrated as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk tandatangan yang sah, ketepatan algoritma DSA mudah ditunjukkan "
"seperti berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the signer's end: $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q \\implies k = ((H(m) + "
"xr)s^{-1})~mod~q $\n"
msgstr ""
"Di pihak penandatangan: $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q \\implies k = ((H(m)"
" + xr)s^{-1})~mod~q $\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Considering the right-hand side of the latter equality, a verifier can "
"compute $s^{-1}, H(m)$ because $s, q, m, H$ are public information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memandangkan bahagian kanan kesamaan yang terakhir, pengesah boleh mengira "
"$s^{-1}, H(m)$ kerana $s, q, m, H$ adalah maklumat awam.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, the verifier computes $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$ and $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q = "
"H(m)s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh itu, pengesah mengira $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$ dan $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q = "
"H(m)s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The verifier also computes $u_2 = rw~mod~q = rs^{-1}~mod~q$ as $r$ is also "
"public.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengesah juga mengira $u_2 = rw~mod~q = rs^{-1}~mod~q$ kerana $r$ juga "
"awam.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Note that $k = (u_1 + xu_2)~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa $k = (u_1 + xu_2)~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, a verifier does not have access to $x$ as it is the signer's "
"private key, so $k$ itself cannot be directly computed.  - The scheme "
"instead relies on the fact that even as the verifier cannot compute $k$, "
"with a legitimate signer, the verifier should instead be able to re-compute "
"$(g^k~mod~p)~mod~q = r$ with the help of the signer's public key $y = "
"g^{x}~mod~p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walau bagaimanapun, pengesah tidak mempunyai akses kepada $x$ kerana ia "
"adalah kunci peribadi penandatangan, jadi $k$ itu sendiri tidak boleh dikira"
" secara langsung. - Skim ini sebaliknya bergantung pada hakikat bahawa "
"walaupun pengesah tidak dapat mengira $k$, dengan penandatangan yang sah, "
"pengesah sepatutnya mampu mengira semula $(g^k~mod~p)~mod~q = r$ dengan "
"bantuan kunci awam penandatangan $y = g^{x}~mod~p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, the verifier computes $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q = "
"(g^{u_1}g^{xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = (g^{u_1+xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = "
"(g^k~mod~p)mod~q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, pengesah mengira $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q = "
"(g^{u_1}g^{xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = (g^{u_1+xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = "
"(g^k~mod~p)mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last equality follows because $g$ has order $q$ and establishes $v = r$ "
"for valid signatures.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kesamaan terakhir berikut kerana $g$ bertertib $q$ dan menetapkan $v = r$ "
"untuk tandatangan yang sah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Illustration of the DSA in Python {#illustration-of-the-dsa-in-python}"
msgstr "Ilustrasi DSA dalam Python {#illustration-of-the-dsa-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this example, we'll use small primes to illustrate the DSA process in a "
"scenario where Alice sends a signed message to Bob. We'll use small integers"
" in this example. A real-world scenario would employ much larger primes on "
"the order of 2048-3072 bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, kita akan menggunakan nombor perdana kecil untuk "
"mengilustrasikan proses DSA dalam senario di mana Alice menghantar mesej "
"bertandatangan kepada Bob. Kita akan menggunakan integer kecil dalam contoh "
"ini. Senario dunia sebenar akan menggunakan nombor perdana yang jauh lebih "
"besar dalam tertib 2048-3072 bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"You can try rerunning this example with different values to see how the algorithm behaves, but ensure you start running from the first cell in this section.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Anda boleh cuba jalankan semula contoh ini dengan nilai berbeza untuk melihat bagaimana algoritma berkelakuan, tetapi pastikan anda mula menjalankan dari sel pertama dalam bahagian ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We start by importing necessary libraries and choosing our parameters.\n"
"The integer parameters $p$, $q$, $g$ are public information, and satisfy the following rules:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mulakan dengan mengimport perpustakaan yang diperlukan dan memilih parameter kita.\n"
"Parameter integer $p$, $q$, $g$ adalah maklumat awam, dan memenuhi peraturan berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$p$, $q$ are both prime\n"
msgstr "$p$, $q$ kedua-duanya perdana\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$(p-1) \\mod\\ q = 0$\n"
msgstr "$(p-1) \\mod\\ q = 0$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$g \\ge 2$\n"
msgstr "$g \\ge 2$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$g \\le (p-2)$\n"
msgstr "$g \\le (p-2)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$g^{(p-1)/q} \\mod\\ p \\neq 1$\n"
msgstr "$g^{(p-1)/q} \\mod\\ p \\neq 1$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next the signer, Alice, generates her private key.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya penandatangan, Alice, menjana kunci peribadinya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key, k (`alice-private-key` in the python code) must satisfy:\n"
" - $k \\ge 2$\n"
" - $k \\le (q-1)$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci peribadi, k (`alice-private-key` dalam kod python) mesti memenuhi:\n"
" - $k \\ge 2$\n"
" - $k \\le (q-1)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice keeps her private key secret.\n"
msgstr "Alice menyimpan kunci peribadinya sebagai rahsia.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice computes her public key using modular exponentiation. Inverting "
"this step to recover the private key is an instance of the DLP, so difficult"
" to compute on classical computers where large primes are used.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, Alice mengira kunci awamnya menggunakan pemangkatan modular. "
"Membalikkan langkah ini untuk mendapatkan semula kunci peribadi adalah "
"contoh DLP, jadi sukar untuk dikira pada komputer klasik apabila perdana "
"besar digunakan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the math explanation above, we know is this can be calculated using the"
" formula:\n"
msgstr ""
"Daripada penjelasan matematik di atas, kita tahu ini boleh dikira "
"menggunakan formula:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$y = g^{x} \\mod\\ p$\n"
msgstr "$y = g^{x} \\mod\\ p$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As usual, Alice makes her public key available over a not-necessarily secret"
" channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti biasa, Alice menjadikan kunci awamnya tersedia melalui saluran yang "
"tidak semestinya rahsia.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now Alice can sign a message.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang Alice boleh menandatangani mesej.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the digital signature scheme, we need to generate a hash $H(m)$ of the "
"message $m$ to be signed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk skim tandatangan digital, kita perlu menjana cincang $H(m)$ bagi mesej"
" $m$ yang akan ditandatangani.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's assume Alice and Bob agree to use a particular hashing algorithm with "
"hash length $N$ equal to the number of bits in $q$. In this simple example, "
"we will bound the outputs of our mock hash function by $q$. The hash "
"function here is trivial, simply generating a random integer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Katakan Alice dan Bob bersetuju untuk menggunakan algoritma pencincangan "
"tertentu dengan panjang cincang $N$ sama dengan bilangan bit dalam $q$. "
"Dalam contoh mudah ini, kita akan membatasi output fungsi cincang tiruan "
"kita dengan $q$. Fungsi cincang di sini adalah trivial, hanya menjana "
"integer rawak.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice needs to generate a random per-message secret number $k$ as well"
" as its multiplicative inverse modulo $q$ to compute the signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya, Alice perlu menjana nombor rahsia rawak setiap mesej $k$ serta "
"songsangan pendaraban modulonya $q$ untuk mengira tandatangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simple brute-force algorithm can be used to compute the modular inverse. "
"However it's better to use one of the built-in Python function `pow` as "
"shown below\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma kekerasan mudah boleh digunakan untuk mengira songsangan modular. "
"Walau bagaimanapun, lebih baik menggunakan salah satu fungsi Python terbina "
"dalam `pow` seperti yang ditunjukkan di bawah\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice can now compute the signature.\n"
msgstr "Alice kini boleh mengira tandatangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$r = (g^{k} \\mod p) \\mod\\ q$\n"
msgstr "$r = (g^{k} \\mod p) \\mod\\ q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr)) \\mod q$\n"
msgstr "$s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr)) \\mod q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that there are some particular conditions that will require us to "
"choose a different value for $k$ in the case where either $r$ or $s$ compute"
" to $0$. In this case we will generate a new value and repeat.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa terdapat beberapa syarat tertentu yang akan memerlukan "
"kita memilih nilai berbeza untuk $k$ dalam kes di mana sama ada $r$ atau $s$"
" mengira kepada $0$. Dalam kes ini kita akan menjana nilai baru dan ulang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice broadcasts the message and her signature to the receiver or verifier, "
"Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice menyiarkan mesej dan tandatangannya kepada penerima atau pengesah, "
"Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob has previously intercepted Alice's public key and can now verify the "
"signature to authenticate her message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob sebelum ini telah memperoleh kunci awam Alice dan kini boleh mengesahkan"
" tandatangan untuk mengesahkan mesejnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To do so, he performs some checks, and then re-generates a hash of Alice's broadcast message and computes the auxiliary quantities $w, u_1, u_2$ and $v$.\n"
"- $0 < r < q$\n"
"- $0 < s < q$\n"
"- $w = s^{-1} \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{1} = H(m) . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{2} = r . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $v = (g^{u1}y^{u2} \\mod\\ p) \\mod\\ q$\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk melakukannya, dia melakukan beberapa semakan, kemudian menjana semula cincang mesej siaran Alice dan mengira kuantiti tambahan $w, u_1, u_2$ dan $v$.\n"
"- $0 < r < q$\n"
"- $0 < s < q$\n"
"- $w = s^{-1} \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{1} = H(m) . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{2} = r . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $v = (g^{u1}y^{u2} \\mod\\ p) \\mod\\ q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob checks if $v$ equals $r$. If they are equal, then the signature"
" is verified.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, Bob menyemak sama ada $v$ bersamaan $r$. Jika ia sama, maka "
"tandatangan disahkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Security of the DSA {#security-of-the-dsa}"
msgstr "Keselamatan DSA {#security-of-the-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With classical computing, the security of the DSA can be influenced by "
"several factors:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan pengkomputeran klasik, keselamatan DSA boleh dipengaruhi oleh "
"beberapa faktor:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key size**: As always, key size provides basic protection against brute "
"force attacks. Modern applications that use DSA use key sizes of at least "
"2048 bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Saiz kunci**: Seperti biasa, saiz kunci memberikan perlindungan asas "
"terhadap serangan kekerasan. Aplikasi moden yang menggunakan DSA menggunakan"
" saiz kunci sekurang-kurangnya 2048 bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quality of $k$**: In DSA, each signature needs a unique, random, and "
"secret $k$ value (see above). The uniqueness, entropy, and secrecy of $k$ "
"are critical, and weakness in any of these aspects could lead to the private"
" key $x$ being compromised. The random number generators used for generating"
" $k$ need to be secure themselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kualiti $k$**: Dalam DSA, setiap tandatangan memerlukan nilai $k$ yang "
"unik, rawak, dan rahsia (lihat di atas). Keunikan, entropi, dan kerahsiaan "
"$k$ adalah kritikal, dan kelemahan dalam mana-mana aspek ini boleh "
"menyebabkan kunci peribadi $x$ terkompromi. Penjana nombor rawak yang "
"digunakan untuk menjana $k$ perlu selamat dengan sendirinya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Hash function strength**: Since DSA uses a hash function as part of the "
"signature generation and verification process, a weak hash function could "
"compromise the security of the digital signature. For example, the use of "
"SHA-1 with DSA is deprecated and SHA-2 or higher is recommended.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kekuatan fungsi cincang**: Memandangkan DSA menggunakan fungsi cincang "
"sebagai sebahagian daripada proses penjanaan dan pengesahan tandatangan, "
"fungsi cincang yang lemah boleh mengkompromi keselamatan tandatangan "
"digital. Contohnya, penggunaan SHA-1 dengan DSA sudah lapuk dan SHA-2 atau "
"lebih tinggi disyorkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to these, robust DSA implementation should also guard against "
"other types of attacks that target asymmetric key cryptography as previously"
" outlined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain ini, implementasi DSA yang kukuh juga harus melindungi daripada jenis"
" serangan lain yang menyasar kriptografi kunci asimetri seperti yang "
"digariskan sebelumnya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and DSA {#authenticated-key-"
"exchange-with-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"
msgstr ""
"Pertukaran kunci disahkan dengan Diffie-Hellman dan DSA {#authenticated-key-"
"exchange-with-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Modern network security protocols, such as [Transport Layer Security "
"(TLS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531)"
" and many others, involve combining the functionalities of key exchange and "
"authentication. In the context of Diffie-Hellman, authentication is needed "
"to guard against MITM attacks. In the following code cells, we illustrate an"
" example where Alice and Bob perform an authenticated key exchange by "
"combining the Diffie-Hellman and DSA protocols. For this, we will use the "
"`cryptography` Python library.\n"
msgstr ""
"Protokol keselamatan rangkaian moden, seperti [Transport Layer Security "
"(TLS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531)"
" dan banyak lagi, melibatkan penggabungan fungsi pertukaran kunci dan "
"pengesahan. Dalam konteks Diffie-Hellman, pengesahan diperlukan untuk "
"melindungi daripada serangan MITM. Dalam sel kod berikut, kita "
"mengilustrasikan contoh di mana Alice dan Bob melakukan pertukaran kunci "
"yang disahkan dengan menggabungkan protokol Diffie-Hellman dan DSA. Untuk "
"ini, kita akan menggunakan perpustakaan Python `cryptography`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 2. Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and "
"DSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/auth_key_exchange.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Rajah 2. Pertukaran kunci disahkan dengan Diffie-Hellman dan "
"DSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/auth_key_exchange.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 2. Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and DSA*\n"
"First, Alice and Bob agree on a set of DH parameters and generate a set of DH public-private key pairs.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Rajah 2. Pertukaran kunci disahkan dengan Diffie-Hellman dan DSA*\n"
"Pertama, Alice dan Bob bersetuju pada set parameter DH dan menjana set pasangan kunci awam-peribadi DH.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The DH public keys are broadcast. Next, both Alice and Bob each generate a "
"separate key pair for use with DSA. These keys will in turn be used to sign "
"the DH public keys to be exchanged.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci awam DH disiarkan. Seterusnya, Alice dan Bob masing-masing menjana "
"pasangan kunci berasingan untuk digunakan dengan DSA. Kunci-kunci ini pula "
"akan digunakan untuk menandatangani kunci awam DH yang akan ditukar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice signs her DH public key using her DSA private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice menandatangani kunci awam DH-nya menggunakan kunci peribadi DSA-nya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, Bob signs his DH public key using his DSA private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Begitu juga, Bob menandatangani kunci awam DH-nya menggunakan kunci peribadi"
" DSA-nya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The DH public keys and corresponding signatures are now broadcast by both "
"Alice and Bob. Having received their counterparty's public key and "
"signature, each party then verifies the signature is valid. This way, a MITM"
" attack can be prevented, as Alice, for instance, knows that Bob's DH public"
" key was indeed signed by Bob and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci awam DH dan tandatangan yang sepadan kini disiarkan oleh Alice dan "
"Bob. Setelah menerima kunci awam dan tandatangan rakan sejawat mereka, "
"setiap pihak kemudian mengesahkan bahawa tandatangan adalah sah. Dengan cara"
" ini, serangan MITM dapat dicegah, kerana Alice, misalnya, tahu bahawa kunci"
" awam DH Bob memang telah ditandatangani oleh Bob dan begitu juga "
"sebaliknya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following signature verification, Alice and Bob generate the shared secret, "
"which completes the key exchange.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selepas pengesahan tandatangan, Alice dan Bob menjana rahsia dikongsi, yang "
"melengkapkan pertukaran kunci.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optionally, for additional security, Alice and Bob can use a specialized key"
" derivation function such as *HKDF* to generate a more secure symmetric key "
"from their shared secret using *key stretching* techniques.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara pilihan, untuk keselamatan tambahan, Alice dan Bob boleh menggunakan "
"fungsi derivasi kunci khusus seperti *HKDF* untuk menjana kunci simetri yang"
" lebih selamat daripada rahsia dikongsi mereka menggunakan teknik *key "
"stretching*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking Diffie-Hellman and DSA {#breaking-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"
msgstr "Memecahkan Diffie-Hellman dan DSA {#breaking-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both the [Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) and "
"[DSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" protocols involve the generation of public keys of the form $ y = "
"g^{x}~mod~p$, where the private key $x$ is the discrete logarithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua-dua protokol [Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) dan "
"[DSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" melibatkan penjanaan kunci awam dalam bentuk $ y = g^{x}~mod~p$, di mana "
"kunci peribadi $x$ ialah logaritma diskret.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An attacker who can solve an instance of the DLP can expose the private key "
"of one of the two parties and, by combining it with the public key of the "
"second party, get access to the shared secret. In the case of DSA, an "
"attacker who can solve the DLP can recover the signer's private key, voiding"
" the basic premise of a digital signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penyerang yang boleh menyelesaikan satu contoh DLP boleh mendedahkan kunci "
"peribadi salah satu pihak dan, dengan menggabungkannya dengan kunci awam "
"pihak kedua, mendapat akses kepada rahsia bersama. Dalam kes DSA, penyerang "
"yang boleh menyelesaikan DLP boleh mendapatkan semula kunci peribadi "
"penandatangan, menggugurkan premis asas tandatangan digital.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On classical computing systems, the DLP is believed not to have a "
"polynomial-time solution. But as shown by Peter Shor in his [original 1994 "
"paper](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), Shor's algorithm also "
"solves the DLP in polynomial-time on quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada sistem pengkomputeran klasik, DLP dipercayai tidak mempunyai "
"penyelesaian masa-polinomial. Tetapi seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh Peter "
"Shor dalam [kertas asal 1994](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) "
"beliau, algoritma Shor juga menyelesaikan DLP dalam masa-polinomial pada "
"komputer kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm and the discrete logarithm problem {#shors-algorithm-and-"
"the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Shor dan masalah logaritma diskret {#shors-algorithm-and-the-"
"discrete-logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm is able to solve the discrete logarithm problem in "
"polynomial time. It primarily achieves its efficiency by using quantum "
"algorithms which can find the period of a function which depends on the "
"input to the problem - which is then combined with more conventional "
"operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Shor mampu menyelesaikan masalah logaritma diskret dalam masa "
"polinomial. Ia mencapai kecekapannya terutamanya dengan menggunakan "
"algoritma kuantum yang boleh mencari tempoh suatu fungsi yang bergantung "
"pada input kepada masalah — yang kemudiannya digabungkan dengan operasi yang"
" lebih konvensional.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of Shor's algorithm\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Butiran matematik algoritma Shor\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm provides an efficient solution to the DLP by mapping it to "
"a more general problem in group theory known as the [hidden subgroup "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hidden_subgroup_problem)"
" (HSP).\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Shor menyediakan penyelesaian cekap kepada DLP dengan memetakannya"
" kepada masalah yang lebih umum dalam teori kumpulan yang dikenali sebagai "
"[masalah subkumpulan "
"tersembunyi](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hidden_subgroup_problem)"
" (HSP).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the HSP, one is given an algebraic group $G$ and a function $f: G "
"\\rightarrow X$  from $G$ to some set $X$ such that $f$ is constant on each "
"coset of some subgroup $H$ of $G$ (and distinct on different cosets). Then, "
"the task is to determine $H$. It is known that quantum computers can solve "
"the HSP on finite Abelian groups in time polynomial in $log~|G|$ where $|G|$"
" is the group order.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam HSP, seseorang diberi kumpulan algebra $G$ dan fungsi $f: G "
"\\rightarrow X$ dari $G$ ke beberapa set $X$ sedemikian rupa hingga $f$ "
"adalah malar pada setiap koset bagi suatu subkumpulan $H$ daripada $G$ (dan "
"berbeza pada koset yang berlainan). Kemudian, tugasnya adalah untuk "
"menentukan $H$. Diketahui bahawa komputer kuantum boleh menyelesaikan HSP "
"pada kumpulan Abelian terhingga dalam masa polinomial dalam $log~|G|$ di "
"mana $|G|$ ialah peringkat kumpulan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the case of the integer DLP discussed in this lesson, the mapping to the "
"HSP is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kes DLP integer yang dibincangkan dalam pelajaran ini, pemetaan kepada"
" HSP adalah seperti berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $p$ be a prime and consider the DLP given by $ y = g^r~mod~p$ where $g$ "
"is a generator of $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$. Since $g^{p-1} \\equiv "
"1~mod~p$, $g$ has order $p-1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Biar $p$ ialah nombor perdana dan pertimbangkan DLP yang diberikan oleh $ y "
"= g^r~mod~p$ di mana $g$ ialah penjana $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$. Oleh "
"kerana $g^{p-1} \\equiv 1~mod~p$, $g$ mempunyai peringkat $p-1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose $G = \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ where "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ is the group of integers modulo $(p-1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih $G = \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ di mana "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ ialah kumpulan integer modulo $(p-1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose $f : G \\rightarrow (\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ given as $f(a, b) = "
"g^a y^{-b}~mod~p \\equiv g^{a-rb}~mod~p$ .\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih $f : G \\rightarrow (\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ yang diberikan sebagai "
"$f(a, b) = g^a y^{-b}~mod~p \\equiv g^{a-rb}~mod~p$ .\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The kernel of $f$ is then the subgroup $H_0 = \\langle (r, 1) \\rangle = "
"\\{(a,b) \\in G | f(a,b) \\equiv 1~mod~p\\} = \\{ (a, b) \\in G | a - rb "
"\\equiv 0~mod~(p-1)\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kernel $f$ kemudiannya ialah subkumpulan $H_0 = \\langle (r, 1) \\rangle = "
"\\{(a,b) \\in G | f(a,b) \\equiv 1~mod~p\\} = \\{ (a, b) \\in G | a - rb "
"\\equiv 0~mod~(p-1)\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$f$ is constant on the cosets $(\\delta, 0) + H_0$ and \"hides\" the "
"subgroup $H_0$ setting up an HSP.\n"
msgstr ""
"$f$ adalah malar pada koset $(\\delta, 0) + H_0$ dan \"menyembunyikan\" "
"subkumpulan $H_0$ yang menyediakan satu HSP.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the above, Shor's quantum algorithm for the integer DLP uses a quantum"
" oracle to evaluate the function $f$ on a state representing a uniform "
"superposition over $G$, and then uses the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A "
"quantum algorithm that can be used to find periodic patterns. Named after "
"the Fourier transform in classical physics which can split a signal into a "
"set of sine waves.\">quantum Fourier transform</DefinitionTooltip> and "
"measurements with <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum algorithm used "
"to estimate phase in qubits, named after phase estimation in classical "
"physics.\">phase estimation</DefinitionTooltip> to produce quantum states "
"that allow for the identification of the generator $(r, 1)$ of $H_0$. From "
"this, $r$, the discrete logarithm of interest, can be extracted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berdasarkan perkara di atas, algoritma kuantum Shor untuk DLP integer "
"menggunakan oracle kuantum untuk menilai fungsi $f$ pada suatu keadaan yang "
"mewakili superposisi seragam merentasi $G$, kemudian menggunakan "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum algorithm that can be used to find"
" periodic patterns. Named after the Fourier transform in classical physics "
"which can split a signal into a set of sine waves.\">transformasi Fourier "
"kuantum</DefinitionTooltip> dan pengukuran dengan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm used to estimate phase in qubits, named "
"after phase estimation in classical physics.\">anggaran "
"fasa</DefinitionTooltip> untuk menghasilkan keadaan kuantum yang membolehkan"
" pengenalan penjana $(r, 1)$ bagi $H_0$. Daripada ini, $r$, iaitu logaritma "
"diskret yang dikehendaki, boleh diekstrak.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Shor's original paper](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) has a "
"detailed description of the algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Kertas asal Shor](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) mempunyai "
"penerangan terperinci tentang algoritma tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Elliptic curve cryptography {#elliptic-curve-cryptography}"
msgstr "Kriptografi lengkung eliptik {#elliptic-curve-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[*Elliptic curve cryptography "
"(ECC)*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993), based on the mathematics of [*elliptic"
" "
"curves*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664),"
" offers a powerful approach to asymmetric key cryptography. ECC is known to "
"provide a similar level of security as methods such as RSA but with shorter "
"keys, making it more efficient and particularly well suited to systems with "
"limited resources, such as embedded systems and mobile devices, where the "
"[storage and computational savings of smaller key sizes are highly "
"desirable](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"
msgstr ""
"[*Kriptografi lengkung eliptik "
"(ECC)*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993), berdasarkan matematik [*lengkung "
"eliptik*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664),"
" menawarkan pendekatan yang berkuasa kepada kriptografi kunci asimetri. ECC "
"diketahui menyediakan tahap keselamatan yang serupa dengan kaedah seperti "
"RSA tetapi dengan kunci yang lebih pendek, menjadikannya lebih cekap dan "
"amat sesuai untuk sistem dengan sumber terhad, seperti sistem tertanam dan "
"peranti mudah alih, di mana [penjimatan storan dan pengiraan daripada saiz "
"kunci yang lebih kecil sangat "
"diingini](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Basic principles of elliptic curve cryptography {#basic-principles-of-"
"elliptic-curve-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Prinsip asas kriptografi lengkung eliptik {#basic-principles-of-elliptic-"
"curve-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An elliptic curve is typically of the form $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ with a few interesting properties.\n"
"* It is horizontally symmetric. So for any point $(x,y)$ on the curve, it's reflection $(x,-y)$ is also on the curve\n"
"* Any non-vertical strain line will only intersect the curve at a maximum of three points\n"
msgstr ""
"Lengkung eliptik biasanya berbentuk $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ dengan beberapa sifat yang menarik.\n"
"* Ia simetri secara mendatar. Jadi untuk mana-mana titik $(x,y)$ pada lengkung, pantulannya $(x,-y)$ juga berada pada lengkung\n"
"* Mana-mana garis lurus bukan tegak hanya akan bersilang dengan lengkung pada maksimum tiga titik\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 1. Operations of addition and point doubling on an elliptic curve. "
"Facet 1 defines <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Facet 2 illustrates point doubling <b>2Q "
"= -P</b>. Facet 3 defines the additive inverse of a point as its reflection "
"about the x-axis i.e, <b>P = -Q</b> ](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/ECCfig.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 1. Operations of addition and point doubling on an elliptic curve. "
"Facet 1 defines <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Facet 2 illustrates point doubling <b>2Q "
"= -P</b>. Facet 3 defines the additive inverse of a point as its reflection "
"about the x-axis i.e, <b>P = -Q</b> ](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/ECCfig.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 1. Operations of addition and point doubling on an elliptic curve. "
"Facet 1 defines <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Facet 2 illustrates point doubling <b>2Q "
"= -P</b>. Facet 3 defines the additive inverse of a point as its reflection "
"about the x-axis i.e, <b>P = -Q</b>*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Rajah 1. Operasi penambahan dan penggandaan titik pada lengkung eliptik. "
"Faset 1 mentakrifkan <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Faset 2 menggambarkan penggandaan "
"titik <b>2Q = -P</b>. Faset 3 mentakrifkan songsang aditif suatu titik "
"sebagai pantulannya pada paksi-x, iaitu <b>P = -Q</b>*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve cryptography makes use of applying a series of arithmetic "
"operations to points on the curve. Each effectively navigates to a new point"
" on the curve. This is a simple process to follow in one direction, and with"
" shorter key sizes is more efficient than other algorithms like RSA, but "
"trying to reverse this is very difficult, hence its application to "
"cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kriptografi lengkung eliptik menggunakan siri operasi aritmetik yang "
"dikenakan pada titik-titik pada lengkung. Setiap operasi secara berkesan "
"menavigasi ke titik baru pada lengkung. Ini adalah proses yang mudah untuk "
"diikuti dalam satu arah, dan dengan saiz kunci yang lebih pendek ia lebih "
"cekap daripada algoritma lain seperti RSA, tetapi cuba membalikkan proses "
"ini adalah sangat sukar, maka itulah sebabnya ia digunakan dalam "
"kriptografi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical principles of elliptic curve cryptography\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Prinsip matematik kriptografi lengkung eliptik\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An [elliptic "
"curve](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664)"
" over an algebraic field $K$ is defined by a mathematical equation, "
"typically in the form $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ with the coefficients $a, b \\in "
"K$ and describes points $(x, y) \\in K \\otimes K$ with the additional "
"requirement that the curve have no kinks or self-intersections.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Lengkung "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664)"
" merentasi medan algebra $K$ ditakrifkan oleh persamaan matematik, biasanya "
"dalam bentuk $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ dengan pekali $a, b \\in K$ dan "
"menerangkan titik-titik $(x, y) \\in K \\otimes K$ dengan keperluan tambahan"
" bahawa lengkung tidak mempunyai bengkokan atau persilangan sendiri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The properties of elliptic curves allow for operations of \"addition\" and "
"\"scalar multiplication\" to be defined involving points on the curve.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sifat lengkung eliptik membolehkan operasi \"penambahan\" dan \"pendaraban "
"skalar\" ditakrifkan melibatkan titik-titik pada lengkung.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Addition**: If $P$ and $Q$ are two points on an elliptic curve, then $P + "
"Q$ describes a unique third point identified as follows: Draw the line that "
"intersects $P$ and $Q$ and find the third point, $R$, at which the line "
"intersects the curve again. We then define $P + Q =  −R$, the point opposite"
" $R$ reflected through the $x$-axis (see figure below) . When the line "
"through $P, Q$ does not intersect the curve at any finite $(x, y)$, we say "
"it intersects the curve at the point at infinity $\\mathbf{O}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Penambahan**: Jika $P$ dan $Q$ ialah dua titik pada lengkung eliptik, maka"
" $P + Q$ menerangkan titik ketiga yang unik yang dikenalpasti seperti "
"berikut: Lukis garis yang bersilang dengan $P$ dan $Q$ dan cari titik "
"ketiga, $R$, di mana garis itu bersilang dengan lengkung semula. Kita "
"kemudiannya mentakrifkan $P + Q = −R$, iaitu titik bertentangan dengan $R$ "
"yang dipantulkan melalui paksi-$x$ (lihat rajah di bawah). Apabila garis "
"melalui $P, Q$ tidak bersilang dengan lengkung pada mana-mana $(x, y)$ "
"terhingga, kita katakan ia bersilang dengan lengkung pada titik di infiniti "
"$\\mathbf{O}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve addition satisfies algebraic **group** properties with the "
"point at infinity as the additive identity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penambahan lengkung eliptik memenuhi sifat **kumpulan** algebra dengan titik"
" di infiniti sebagai identiti aditif.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Doubling and scalar multiplication:** The operation of point doubling "
"which corresponds to scalar multiplication by $2$ is obtained by setting $P "
"= Q$ in the addition operation and graphically involves the tangent line at "
"$P$. General scalar multiplication by an integer $n$ defined as $nP =  P + P"
" + ...~n$ times is obtained by repeated doubling and addition.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Penggandaan dan pendaraban skalar:** Operasi penggandaan titik yang "
"sepadan dengan pendaraban skalar sebanyak $2$ diperoleh dengan menetapkan $P"
" = Q$ dalam operasi penambahan dan secara grafik melibatkan garis tangen "
"pada $P$. Pendaraban skalar umum dengan integer $n$ yang ditakrifkan sebagai"
" $nP = P + P + ...~n$ kali diperoleh melalui penggandaan dan penambahan "
"berulang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve discrete logarithm problem {#elliptic-curve-discrete-"
"logarithm-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Masalah logaritma diskret lengkung eliptik {#elliptic-curve-discrete-"
"logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The elliptic curve discrete logarithm problem (ECDLP) has many similarities "
"to the discrete logarithm problem discussed previously, being based around "
"the challenges of finding factors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah logaritma diskret lengkung eliptik (ECDLP) mempunyai banyak "
"persamaan dengan masalah logaritma diskret yang dibincangkan sebelum ini, "
"kerana ia juga berasaskan cabaran mencari faktor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation of [scalar multiplication on elliptic "
"curves](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve_point_multiplication&oldid=1145917191)"
" allows for the definition of the [elliptic curve discrete logarithm "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993):\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi [pendaraban skalar pada lengkung "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve_point_multiplication&oldid=1145917191)"
" membolehkan [masalah logaritma diskret lengkung "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993) ditakrifkan:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given points $P, Q$ on an elliptic curve such that $Q = nP$, determine "
"$n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberi titik $P, Q$ pada lengkung eliptik sedemikian rupa hingga $Q = nP$, "
"tentukan $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This problem is known to be intractable on classical computers for large $n$"
" and provides a basis for cryptographic security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah ini diketahui tidak boleh diselesaikan pada komputer klasik untuk "
"$n$ yang besar dan menjadi asas kepada keselamatan kriptografi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of ECDLP\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Penerangan matematik ECDLP\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve cryptography is primarily based on the ECDLP formulated on "
"certain algebraic **finite fields**. In 1999, NIST recommended ten finite "
"fields for use in ECC. These are:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kriptografi lengkung eliptik terutamanya berdasarkan ECDLP yang "
"diformulasikan pada **medan terhingga** algebra tertentu. Pada tahun 1999, "
"NIST mengesyorkan sepuluh medan terhingga untuk digunakan dalam ECC. Ini "
"adalah:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Five **prime fields** $\\mathbb {F} _{p}$ for primes $p$ of size $\\{192, "
"224, 256, 384, 521\\}$ bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lima **medan perdana** $\\mathbb {F} _{p}$ untuk nombor perdana $p$ bersaiz "
"$\\{192, 224, 256, 384, 521\\}$ bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Five **binary fields** $\\mathbb {F} _{2^{n}}$ for $n \\in \\{163, 233, 283,"
" 409, 571\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lima **medan binari** $\\mathbb {F} _{2^{n}}$ untuk $n \\in \\{163, 233, "
"283, 409, 571\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the above setup, an ECC-based asymmetric key cryptosystem in the case "
"of **prime fields** may be specified as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan persediaan di atas, sistem kriptografi kunci asimetri berasaskan ECC "
"dalam kes **medan perdana** boleh ditentukan seperti berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a $p$ from the NIST-recommended list of values to specify $\\mathbb "
"{F} _{p}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih $p$ daripada senarai nilai yang disyorkan NIST untuk menentukan "
"$\\mathbb {F} _{p}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Select parameters $a, b$ of the elliptic curve.\n"
msgstr "Pilih parameter $a, b$ bagi lengkung eliptik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a **base point** $G$ which \"generates\" a cyclic subgroup on the "
"curve with order $n$; that is, the smallest integer such that $nG = "
"\\mathbf{O}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih **titik asas** $G$ yang \"menjana\" subkumpulan kitaran pada lengkung "
"dengan peringkat $n$; iaitu integer terkecil sedemikian rupa hingga $nG = "
"\\mathbf{O}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the **cofactor** $h = |E(\\mathbb {F} _{p})|/n$ where $|E(\\mathbb"
" {F} _{p})|$ is the number of points on the curve. $h$ is typically a small "
"integer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kira **kofaktor** $h = |E(\\mathbb {F} _{p})|/n$ di mana $|E(\\mathbb {F} "
"_{p})|$ ialah bilangan titik pada lengkung. $h$ biasanya ialah integer "
"kecil.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **domain parameters** $(p, a, b, G, n, h)$ allow the specification of "
"asymmetric keys in this way:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Parameter domain** $(p, a, b, G, n, h)$ membolehkan spesifikasi kunci "
"asimetri dengan cara ini:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key is a randomly chosen integer $d$ with as many bits as in the"
" prime $p$. It should be kept secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci peribadi ialah integer rawak $d$ dengan bilangan bit yang sama dengan "
"nombor perdana $p$. Ia perlu dirahsiakan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The public key is the result of \"multiplying\" the base point $G$ by the "
"private key $d$. This is typically denoted as $Q = dG$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci awam ialah hasil \"pendaraban\" titik asas $G$ dengan kunci peribadi "
"$d$. Ini biasanya dinotasikan sebagai $Q = dG$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recovering $d$ is equivalent to solving the ECDLP, which is assumed to be "
"intractable for large $d$. The ECDLP therefore forms the basis for key "
"exchange and digital signature schemes in direct analogy with the Diffie-"
"Hellman and DSA schemes defined over $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ discussed "
"previously.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mendapatkan semula $d$ bersamaan dengan menyelesaikan ECDLP, yang dianggap "
"tidak boleh diselesaikan untuk $d$ yang besar. Oleh itu ECDLP menjadi asas "
"kepada skema pertukaran kunci dan tandatangan digital secara analog langsung"
" dengan skema Diffie-Hellman dan DSA yang ditakrifkan merentasi "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ yang dibincangkan sebelum ini.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Key exchange with ECC {#key-exchange-with-ecc}"
msgstr "Pertukaran kunci dengan ECC {#key-exchange-with-ecc}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One of the primary uses of ECC is in the key exchange protocol known as "
"[elliptic curve Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman&oldid=1160050860) (ECDH). In ECDH, each party "
"generates a private-public key pair and then exchanges public keys. Each "
"party then uses their own private key and the other party's public key to "
"compute a shared secret, which can be used as the key for symmetric "
"encryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"Salah satu kegunaan utama ECC ialah dalam protokol pertukaran kunci yang "
"dikenali sebagai [Diffie-Hellman lengkung "
"eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman&oldid=1160050860) (ECDH). Dalam ECDH, setiap "
"pihak menjana pasangan kunci peribadi-awam dan kemudian bertukar kunci awam."
" Setiap pihak kemudian menggunakan kunci peribadi mereka sendiri dan kunci "
"awam pihak lain untuk mengira rahsia bersama, yang boleh digunakan sebagai "
"kunci untuk penyulitan simetri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While it's relatively easy to perform point addition on an elliptic curve "
"and derive a public key from a private key, it's computationally infeasible "
"to reverse the process and derive a private key from a public key. This "
"\"one-way\" behavior provides the security of the ECDH key exchange.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun agak mudah untuk melakukan penambahan titik pada lengkung eliptik "
"dan mendapatkan kunci awam daripada kunci peribadi, ia secara pengiraan "
"tidak boleh dilaksanakan untuk membalikkan proses dan mendapatkan kunci "
"peribadi daripada kunci awam. Tingkah laku \"sehala\" ini menyediakan "
"keselamatan pertukaran kunci ECDH.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we will illustrate an example of how one might perform an ECDH key "
"exchange using Python and the library `cryptography`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita akan menggambarkan contoh bagaimana seseorang boleh melakukan "
"pertukaran kunci ECDH menggunakan Python dan pustaka `cryptography`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Digital signatures with ECC {#digital-signatures-with-ecc}"
msgstr "Tandatangan digital dengan ECC {#digital-signatures-with-ecc}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ECC can also be used to generate digital signatures using the [Elliptic "
"Curve Digital Signature "
"Algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA). In ECDSA, the signer creates a signature using their private key, "
"and others can verify the signature using the signer's public key. Just like"
" with ECDH, the security of ECDSA relies on the ECDLP. It's computationally "
"infeasible for someone to forge a signature without access to the signer's "
"private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"ECC juga boleh digunakan untuk menjana tandatangan digital menggunakan "
"[Algoritma Tandatangan Digital Lengkung "
"Eliptik](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA). Dalam ECDSA, penandatangan mencipta tandatangan menggunakan kunci "
"peribadi mereka, dan orang lain boleh mengesahkan tandatangan menggunakan "
"kunci awam penandatangan. Sama seperti ECDH, keselamatan ECDSA bergantung "
"pada ECDLP. Adalah tidak boleh dilaksanakan secara pengiraan bagi seseorang "
"untuk memalsukan tandatangan tanpa akses kepada kunci peribadi "
"penandatangan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following is an example of a simple sign-and-verify transaction using "
"ECDSA with Python and `cryptography`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut ialah contoh transaksi tanda-dan-sahkan yang mudah menggunakan ECDSA"
" dengan Python dan `cryptography`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above code, if one modifies the message after it has been signed, the"
" verification will fail, providing a guarantee of authenticity and integrity"
" for the message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kod di atas, jika seseorang mengubah mesej selepas ia ditandatangani, "
"pengesahan akan gagal, memberikan jaminan keaslian dan integriti untuk mesej"
" tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking ECDH and ECDSA {#breaking-ecdh-and-ecdsa}"
msgstr "Memecahkan ECDH dan ECDSA {#breaking-ecdh-and-ecdsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In an analogous way to the integer discrete logarithm problem, the ECDLP "
"turns out to be hard on classical computers but has an efficient solution on"
" quantum computers once again via Shor's algorithm. We refer you to recent "
"literature for a discussion related to [generalizing Shor's algorithm to the"
" ECDLP case](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-89432-0_8).\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara analog dengan masalah logaritma diskret integer, ECDLP ternyata sukar"
" pada komputer klasik tetapi mempunyai penyelesaian cekap pada komputer "
"kuantum sekali lagi melalui algoritma Shor. Kami merujuk anda kepada "
"literatur terkini untuk perbincangan berkaitan [pengitlakan algoritma Shor "
"kepada kes ECDLP](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-89432-0_8).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we started by looking at the main characteristics of "
"asymmetric key cryptography (AKC) and discussed basic security "
"considerations that underpin asymmetric cryptosystems. In particular, we "
"introduced the two main applications of AKC — namely, key exchange and "
"digital signatures — both of which are essential components of modern "
"internet-based communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran ini, kita mulakan dengan melihat ciri-ciri utama kriptografi"
" kunci asimetri (AKC) dan membincangkan pertimbangan keselamatan asas yang "
"menyokong sistem kriptografi asimetri. Khususnya, kita memperkenalkan dua "
"aplikasi utama AKC — iaitu, pertukaran kunci dan tandatangan digital — yang "
"kedua-duanya merupakan komponen penting komunikasi berasaskan internet "
"moden.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then looked at the RSA cryptosystem, which since the 1970s, has proven to"
" be of immense value for securing modern digital communications by enabling "
"key exchange and digital signatures within a simple and versatile framework."
" The cryptographic security of RSA with respect to classical computing is "
"based on the hardness of factoring large integers and requires key sizes in "
"the range of 2048 bits to assure the integers used in practical applications"
" are large enough to resist factorization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kemudian melihat sistem kriptografi RSA, yang sejak tahun 1970-an, "
"telah terbukti amat bernilai dalam mengamankan komunikasi digital moden "
"dengan membolehkan pertukaran kunci dan tandatangan digital dalam rangka "
"kerja yang mudah dan serba boleh. Keselamatan kriptografi RSA berkenaan "
"pengkomputeran klasik adalah berdasarkan kesukaran memfaktorkan integer "
"besar dan memerlukan saiz kunci dalam julat 2048 bit untuk memastikan "
"integer yang digunakan dalam aplikasi praktikal cukup besar untuk menahan "
"pemfaktoran.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then looked at Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange and the Digital Signature"
" Algorithm (DSA). The security of these schemes is predicated on the integer"
" discrete logarithm (DLP) problem, the private key being computationally "
"hard to extract given the public key, with no polynomial time solution on "
"classical computers. Use of random and unique keys affords additional "
"security against attacks. Both the integer finite field and elliptic curve "
"variants of the DH and DSA protocols currently find widespread use across "
"many modern digital communications protocols such as "
"[*TLS*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531),"
" "
"[*SSH*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Secure_Shell&oldid=1158549718),"
" and so on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kemudian melihat pertukaran kunci Diffie-Hellman (DH) dan Algoritma "
"Tandatangan Digital (DSA). Keselamatan skema ini bersandar pada masalah "
"logaritma diskret integer (DLP), di mana kunci peribadi sukar diekstrak "
"secara pengiraan berdasarkan kunci awam, tanpa penyelesaian masa polinomial "
"pada komputer klasik. Penggunaan kunci rawak dan unik memberikan keselamatan"
" tambahan terhadap serangan. Kedua-dua varian medan terhingga integer dan "
"lengkung eliptik bagi protokol DH dan DSA pada masa ini digunakan secara "
"meluas merentasi banyak protokol komunikasi digital moden seperti "
"[*TLS*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531),"
" "
"[*SSH*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Secure_Shell&oldid=1158549718),"
" dan lain-lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we looked at Elliptic curve cryptography. With its efficient key "
"size and strong security properties, it currently represents an excellent "
"choice for many cryptographic applications, from key exchange to digital "
"signatures.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya kita melihat kriptografi lengkung eliptik. Dengan saiz kunci yang "
"cekap dan sifat keselamatan yang kukuh, ia kini mewakili pilihan yang "
"cemerlang untuk banyak aplikasi kriptografi, daripada pertukaran kunci "
"hingga tandatangan digital.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All of these algorithms have exposure to attack from quantum algorithms, "
"since solutions can be developed to solve the mathematical problems which "
"acted as a premise in their design. One such example is Shor's algorithm. "
"Therefore they will need to be replaced by quantum-safe asymmetric "
"cryptosystems which are more resilient to attack from quantum - as well as "
"being as safe with classical algorithms. The mathematical problems they rely"
" on can be solved efficiently by quantum computers, necessitating the "
"development of quantum-safe asymmetric cryptosystems that can withstand "
"quantum attacks while maintaining classical security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semua algoritma ini terdedah kepada serangan daripada algoritma kuantum, "
"kerana penyelesaian boleh dibangunkan untuk menyelesaikan masalah matematik "
"yang menjadi premis dalam reka bentuk mereka. Salah satu contoh ialah "
"algoritma Shor. Oleh itu, ia perlu digantikan oleh sistem kriptografi "
"asimetri selamat-kuantum yang lebih tahan kepada serangan dari kuantum — "
"sambil tetap selamat dengan algoritma klasik. Masalah matematik yang mereka "
"bergantung padanya boleh diselesaikan dengan cekap oleh komputer kuantum, "
"memerlukan pembangunan sistem kriptografi asimetri selamat-kuantum yang "
"mampu menahan serangan kuantum sambil mengekalkan keselamatan klasik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A future lesson will look at quantum-safe cryptosystems and discuss the "
"required approach to maintain cryptographic security.\n"
msgstr ""
